hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:
"28057","(28057) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, he said: Retaliation In what is between a man and a woman in the matter of intentionality, in what is between him and himself."
"28058","(28058) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Retaliation between a man and a woman for intentional acts, in every matter."
"28059","(28059) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Hammad; He did not see retaliation between men and women for anything other than one's life.

 The arbitrator said: We have not heard anything about them, and retaliation between them is good."
"28060","(28060) Issa told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The Sunnah passed for a man to hit his wife. So he hurts her not to retaliate against him, and he makes sense for her."
"28061","(28061) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: A woman should not be cut. From her husband"
"28062","(28062) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Ezza, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Concerning a man who forced his wife to have intercourse with her, then he corrected her age. He said: He is guaranteed."
"28063","(28063) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad, he said: There is no retaliation between a man and a woman in what is less than the life. Concerning intentionality."
"28064","(28064) Waki’ told us, saying: Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who slapped his wife, and she came seeking retaliation, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, made retaliation between them, so God sent down God Almighty: {And do not hasten with the Qur’an before its revelation has been decreed to you} And it was revealed: {Men are guardians of women by what God has made abundantly abundantly. each other against each other}"
"28065","(28065) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Qasim bin Al-Fadl Al-Haddani narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ziyad, who said: My maternal grandmother was A son of Othman bin Mazun. When Othman died, Ibn Othman wounded her, so she mentioned that to Omar bin Al-Khattab, and Omar said to him: Give her a share of what you did to her."
"28066","(28066) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The wounds of men and women are equal in age. And the clarifier."
"28067","(28067) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: Urwa al-Bariqi came to me from Omar; The wounds of men and women are equal in age and condition, and above that, the woman’s ransom is equal to half of the man’s blood money."
"28068","(28068) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih; That Hisham bin Hubaira wrote to him asking him, so he wrote to him: The woman’s blood money is half of her blood money. The man, except in the Sunnah and the Muddahah."
"28069","(28069) Waki’ told us, he said: Zakaria and Ibn Abi Layla told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Ali used to say: The woman's diyah in error is half of the man's diyah, as stated by God Almighty.

 Ibn Masoud used to say: A woman’s blood money for a sinner is half of a man’s blood money, except for the Sunnah and the Mudhahih, which are in it. Either way

 Zayd ibn Thabit used to say: A woman’s blood money for a mistake is like a man’s blood money, until it reaches a third of the blood money. His mouth increased to half."
"28070","(28070) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Zaid bin Thabit, that he said: They are equal to One-third"
"28071","(28071) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The wounds of men and women are equal to half, so if they reach Half means half."
"28072","(28072) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: A woman should be sensible. The leg is up to a third, her finger is like his finger, her tooth is like her tooth, her forelock is like her forelock, and her forelock is like her forelock. Like a gurney"
"28073","(28073) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, and Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali, who said: Women’s wounds are equal. And men are in everything."
"28074","(28074) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dhakwan Abi Al-Zanad, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Al-Aziz, he said: Concerning a woman’s clarification, her narration, and her age, the parable of a man in terms of blood money."
"28075","(28075) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: Her movable, And I explained it, and its Sunnah is like a man’s blood money."
"28076","(28076) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Abi Abd al-Rahman, he said: I said to Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab: How many women are there in this? He means the pinky. He said: Ten camels. He said: I said: About these two? He means the pinky and the next. He said: Twenty. He said: I said: So these? He means three. He said: Thirty. He said: I said: What about these? And he gestured to the four. He said: Twenty. He said: I said: When her wounds were painful and her affliction was great, was it the least for her enemies? He said: Are you ethnic? He said: I said: A proven scholar, or an ignorant and learned person. He said: O son of my brother, the Sunnah.

(Malik 8600 Abdul Razzaq 17749)"
"28077","(28077) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Mas’udi told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Utaiba, he said: Sharih wrote to Hisham. Ibn Hubayra: The woman’s blood money is half of the man’s blood money, except for the Sunnah and the Mudhahiyah."
"28078","(28078) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab (h) and on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz; They both said: A man should live with a woman for a third of her blood money, then they would disagree."
"28079","(28079) Abdul Rahim narrated to us, Ibn Abi Aroubah narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: Whoever kills his servant, We will kill him, and whoever kills his servant, We will kill him.

(Abu Dawud 4504, Tirmidhi 1414)"
"28080","(28080) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If he kills his servant intentionally He was killed by it."
"28081","(28081) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Shu`ba narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Abraham, he said: He will be killed because of him."
"28082","(28082) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked the ruling about a man who intentionally kills his slave? He said: I see him being killed with it."
"28083","(28083) Ismail bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abi Farwa, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Hunayn On the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, he said: A man was brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who killed his servant intentionally, and the Messenger of God flogged him. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he removed a hundred lashes, exiled a year, wiped out his shares from the Muslims, but did not kill them.

(Ibn Majah 2664. Daraqutni 143)"
"28084","(28084) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abi Farwa, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; Like him (Bayhaqi 37)"
"28085","(28085) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Amir, who said: If a man kills his slave intentionally, he does not He will be killed with it."
"28086","(28086) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Lahia, on the authority of Khalid ibn Abi Imran, he said: I asked Salim and al-Qasim about A man killed his servant? They said: His punishment is to be killed, but he should not be killed for it."
"28087","(28087) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib; That Abu Bakr and Omar used to say: The master should not kill his servant, but rather he should be beaten and detained for a long time. And his shares are forbidden."
"28088","(28088) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather; Abu Bakr and Omar did not kill a free person by killing a slave."
"28089","(28089) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali and Abdullah, that they said: If A free man kills a slave, so he is a slave to it."
"28090","(28090) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, who said: The slave is killed for the free, and the free for the slave."
"28091","(28091) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: I asked him about A free man killed a slave? He said: He will be killed for it, then I returned to him, and he said: He will be killed for it, then he said: By God, if the people of Yemen gathered against him I would have killed them with it."
"28092","(28092) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, he said: I asked Sa`id bin al-Musayyab about A free man intentionally kills a slave? He said: Kill him, even if the people of Yemen gather against him."
"28093","(28093) Waki’ told us, he said: Ali bin Salih told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Wadhin, he said: I asked Al-Sha’bi about Al-Hurr. Kills a slave intentionally? He said: Kill him as a mean and arrogant person."
"28094","(28094) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: A free man cannot be led by a slave."
"28095","(28095) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: I heard Sufyan saying: A man may be killed for the servant of another, but he should not be killed for his own servant. Just as if he had killed his son, he would not have been killed because of him."
"28096","(28096) Waki’ told us, he said: I heard Sufyan saying: A man should not be killed for his servant, but he should be punished."
"28097","(28097) Abbad told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Zaid; In a fall, he falls and moves. He said: His blood money is complete. Was it readable, or not readable?"
"28098","(28098) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: In the fetus, if it aborts alive, then in it. The blood money, and if it falls dead, then there is a sin in it."
"28099","(28099) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If a man strikes the pregnant woman’s stomach and she miscarries If he is dead, then the slave’s jealousy is in it, or his property is in the slave mother, and if he is alive, then the blood money."
"28100","(28100) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If the fetus begins, then dies In it is the blood money."
"28101","(28101) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A woman gave birth to a son, and his wives witnessed that he had intercourse. He was born alive, but they did not bear witness to the establishment. Shurayh said: The living inherits the dead, then his inheritance was invalidated because he did not They bear witness to the establishment of God."
"28102","(28102) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Jundub al-Qasas, on the authority of Aslam, the client of Omar, on the authority of Omar; He made a ruling regarding the age of a boy if she had a miscarriage before the camel had gaped."
"28103","(28103) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: He is not of the age of a boy if he has no gaps except pain."
"28104","(28104) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Salim, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: If his tooth is correct and does not make a gap, then there is a ruling on it."
"28105","(28105) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ibn Shihab said about a young boy who did not have a tooth broken. Another boy said: He will pay the fine as much as the judge deems appropriate."
"28106","(28106) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: At the age of a boy if he does not gape, he said: He should look. There are people of justice in it, and if it grows, something is made for it, and if it does not grow, it is like a man’s teeth."
"28107","(28107) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, who said: What befalls a crazy person in his state of insanity is the same as his sane person, and what When he woke up, he was arrested."
"28108","(28108) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He said about the insane, the one who has lost his mind, the lunatic, and the one whose affliction is once or twice in the month. He said: If he goes away from that, then he fasts, prays, is sensible, and does something, then it is upon him."
"28109","(28109) Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Dear; He made the crime of the insane equal to that of the sane."
"28110","(28110) Affan told us, he said: Sakhr bin Juwayriyah told us, on the authority of Nafi’; A madman during the time of Ibn al-Zubayr would sometimes wake up, but no harm was seen in him, and his pain would return to him. While he was sleeping with his cousin, he entered the house with a dagger and stabbed his cousin, killing him. Abdullah bin Al-Zubair was judged. That he be stripped of his wealth and given to the family of the murdered person."
"28111","(28111) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a Muslim kills a non-Muslim, he is not liable. Atonement"
"28112","(28112) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Concerning a Muslim who kills a non-Muslim by mistake, he said: Their atonement is the same."
"28113","(28113) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Their expiation is the same."
"28114","(28114) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Yazid al-Ja’fi, on the authority of al-Sha’bi; Regarding a man who is killed and the woman is pardoned, he said: The killer must pay seven-eighths of the blood money."
"28115","(28115) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’; If a woman pardoned her husband’s blood, he said: It became blood money, and the price will be removed from her."
"28116","(28116) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Salih, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos; Concerning a woman whose husband was killed and she pardoned him, he said: Her pardon is permissible, and her share of the blood money will be removed."
"28117","(28117) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is a pardon for every one who has an arrow."
"28118","(28118) He told us about his youth, about his people, about Al-Hakam, and about Hammad; They said about a man who kills a man and the woman is pardoned. They said: Whoever pardons a man or a woman, he will pardon him. Killing"
"28119","(28119) Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Omar, who said: There is no pardon for the husband and wife."
"28120","(28120) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Not for the husband, nor A woman has a pardon for blood, but pardon is only given to the guardians of the murdered person."
"28121","(28121) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: Neither the husband nor the wife has pardon for blood. If one of the heirs pardons him, his pardon is permissible and the blood money is due."
"28122","(28122) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Muslim, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; Concerning a man who was killed and left behind his daughter, his sister, and his two wives, and one of the two women became chaste. Al-Sha’bi said: It is not for the woman. Pardon, except for a woman with close relatives and a share in the inheritance."
"28123","(28123) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed; Omar used to say: The blood money is for the sane woman, and the woman does not inherit anything from her husband’s blood money, until he wrote to her. Al-Dahhak bin Sufyan Al-Kalabi: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, inherited from his wife Ashim Al-Dababi’s blood money. Her husband (Abu Dawud 2919, Tirmidhi 1415)"
"28124","(28124) Yahya bin Zakariya bin Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab said: Omar stood up and asked the people, and said: Who has knowledge of a woman’s inheritance from her husband’s mind? Al-Dahhak bin Sufyan Al-Kalabi got up and said: Enter your cloak until I inform you. So he entered and came to him and said: The Messenger of God wrote to me. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that I bequeath to her woman the foggy hair of her husband’s mind. (Nasa’i 6365)"
"28125","(28125) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who is killed intentionally and some of the heirs pardon him. He said: His wife gets her inheritance from the blood money."
"28126","(28126) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A woman inherits from her husband’s blood."
"28127","(28127) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If reason precedes intentionality, It was an inheritance inherited by the wife and others."
"28128","(28128) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salem, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Omar; He said: Every heir inherits from the blood money, the husband and the wife, whether by mistake or intentionally."
"28129","(28129) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abu Amr Al-Abdi, on the authority of Ali, who said: The blood money will be divided to whomever makes it. Inheritance"
"28130","(28130) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The blood money is for the inheritance, and the mind is for the clan. (Abdul Razzaq 17768)"
"28131","(28131) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabi; He was speaking: that blood money is a way of inheritance."
"28132","(28132) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi (h) and Jahm, on the authority of Ibrahim, they said: The blood money For inheritance."
"28133","(28133) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Book of God is like the rest of his wealth."
"28134","(28134) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Tawus; That his father used to say and decree: That all the heirs inherit from the mind like inheritance."
"28135","(28135) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: Is the mind like the means of inheritance? He said: Yes, I said: And the brothers from the mother inherit from it? He said: Yes."
"28136","(28136) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ali, who said: Ali said: He has wronged the one who did not The maternal brothers inherit from the blood money."
"28137","(28137) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab, on the authority of Omar; He used to inherit blood money from his maternal brothers."
"28138","(28138) Ibn Idris and Ibn Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Brothers from the mother’s side inherit from The blood money, and every heir."
"28139","(28139) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, he said: He wrote in Brothers from the mother: they inherit from the blood money."
"28140","(28140) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: Do brothers inherit from the mother? Meaning, from the mind. He said: Yes."
"28141","(28141) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, who said: I asked Abraham: Do brothers from the mother inherit from the blood money? He said: Yes."
"28142","(28142) Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, who said: I asked Al-Hasan? He said: They have the Book of God."
"28143","(28143) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ali, who said: He who does not inherit has been wronged. Brothers from the mother to the blood-money."
"28144","(28144) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, who said: A man saw a man with his wife and killed her. Then it was brought to Omar, and some of her brothers donated their share to him, so Omar ordered the rest of them to take the blood money."
"28145","(28145) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who killed another man intentionally, and some of his saints forgave him. So that matter was brought up to Omar, and he said to Abdullah: Speak about her, so he said: You are more deserving. To say, O Commander of the Faithful, and Abdullah said: If some of the saints pardon, then there is no retaliation. The stone of the one who pardoned will be dropped from him. They have the rest of the blood money, so Omar said: That is the opinion, and I agreed with what was in my mind."
"28146","(28146) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Issa, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If some of the heirs forgive, the forgiveness follows from that."
"28147","(28147) Abdul-Wahhab bin Ata’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul-Aziz; He said: Whoever pardons will have no share."
"28148","(28148) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: If some of the saints of blood forgive This is the blood money."
"28149","(28149) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The one who pardons is more worthy of blood."
"28150","(28150) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, delivered a letter between the Muhajireen and the Ansar: that they strengthen their strongholds, and that they ransom their suffering with kindness, And reconciliation between Muslims. (Ahmad 271, Abu Ali 2479)"
"28151","(28151) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made He gave the mind of Quraysh to Quraysh, and the mind of the Ansar to the Ansar. (Ibn Hazm 2140)"
"28152","(28152) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, placed the mind on the nerve."
"28153","(28153) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Ali and al-Zubayr disputed over the matter. The loyalty of Safiyah’s loyalists was to Omar, so Omar decided that the inheritance would go to Al-Zubayr, and the inheritance would go to Ali."
"28154","(28154) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar narrated to me, saying: He wrote to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz regarding A man whose master said: We do not make sense of him, so he wrote to the judge: To force them to make sense, for I have no doubt that they would have taken him. inheritance"
"28155","(28155) Kathir bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Jafar bin Burqan; Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote: If he left no relatives except those loyal to him, they would be the people most deserving of his inheritance, so burden them. His mind is as they inherit it."
"28156","(28156) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The inheritance is for the relatives, and the wrongs are upon the one who frees him."
"28157","(28157) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who was emancipated by a people, and whose fathers were emancipated by others. He said: They are inherited by blood relatives, and their crimes are upon the sane ones of their friends."
"28158","(28158) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, who said: The crime of a master upon his sane masters."
"28159","(28159) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Mujahid; A man came to Omar and said: A man who greeted me at my hands died and left behind a thousand dirhams, so I was embarrassed and presented them to you. He said: Have you seen that if he had committed a crime, on whom would it have been? He said: Ali. He said: So his inheritance is yours."
"28160","(28160) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: Reason is upon the one who has the inheritance."
"28161","(28161) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: Do the people refuse to give up on their master? Ata’ said: If his family and people refuse to take care of him, then he is the guardian of the afflicted."
"28162","(28162) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: Umar said about it: If a man appoints another man as his guardian, then he His inheritance, and upon his descendants is his inheritance."
"28163","(28163) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hikam; Concerning a man who took charge of a people, he said: If he abandons them, then he is one of them."
"28164","(28164) Hafs told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Omar, he said: Some of those who came before my father told me, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever is a doctor who practices medicine on a people, and was not known as a doctor before that, and you help, he is liable. He said Abdul Aziz: But it is not an adjective, but rather it is severing the veins and ducking. (Abu Dawud 4577, Musnad 983)"
"28165","(28165) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If the doctor exceeds what he was ordered to do, then he is liable."
"28166","(28166) Muhammad bin Bakr and Omar bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning the doctor collapsing and dying, he said: He is not of sound mind."
"28167","(28167) Ismail told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn al-Ghaz al-Jurshi, on the authority of Abi Qurayh; Omar bin Abdul Aziz included the circumciser."
"28168","(28168) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Yusuf, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir; A woman had a miscarriage with her maid and she helped her, so she died, so he made her liable for the blood money."
"28169","(28169) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Ghaylan bin Jami’ al-Muharbibi, on the authority of Abu Awn al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Shurayh said: The healer is not liable."
"28170","(28170) Waki’ told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, he said: There is no guarantee on the healer."
"28171","(28171) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq narrated to us, saying: I heard Al-Sha’bi saying: He is not a cupper, nor A farrier, and no healer is a guarantee."
"28172","(28172) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir; In a farrier, he removed a fingernail from the eye of a horse, and the horse died. He said: Damn."
"28173","(28173) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih; During his circumcision in Medina, a female slave was circumcised and she died, and Omar said to her: Didn’t you keep such-and-such, and he made her blood money according to I made her wise."
"28174","(28174) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabă; A woman was belittling a slave girl and she helped her, so Omar took her to task and said: Didn’t you leave such-and-such?"
"28175","(28175) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, he said: I said to my father: A man is killed and his blood is pardoned. He said: It is permissible. He said: I said: by mistake, or intentionally? He said: Yes."
"28176","(28176) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to say: If a man pardons his intentional killer before he dies, then it is permissible."
"28177","(28177) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders; That Urwa bin Masoud Al-Thaqafi called his people to God and to His Messenger, and a man from among them shot him with an arrow, and he died and pardoned, so he was raised. That was up to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he permitted his pardon, and said: He is like the companion of Yasin. (Tabarani 12156)"
"28178","(28178) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I heard Ata’ say: Wahhab is the one who kills by mistake. His blood money is for the one who killed him. He only gets a third of it, but it is money to bequeath to him."
"28179","(28179) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Mubarak, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Samak ibn al-Fadl, on the authority of Umar ibn Abdul Aziz, he said: From a third."
"28180","(28180) Ismail bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Abi Zaid narrated to me, on the authority of Nafi’ ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The blood money of one killed during the sacred months will be increased by four thousand, and the killed In the sanctuary, the additional blood money is four thousand, while the value of the sacred blood money is twenty thousand."
"28181","(28181) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Amr bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab; He decided to pay blood money to the people of the village, twelve thousand, and said: “Times will change, and I fear for the rulers after me.” The people of the villages do not have to do anything extra in strengthening their minds, nor in the Sacred Month, nor in the Sacred Mosque, nor in the mind of the people of the villages. There is an increase in it, not an increase in it."
"28182","(28182) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of his father; Othman decided that a blood money and a third of the blood money should be paid for a woman who was killed in the Sanctuary."
"28183","(28183) Muhammad bin Bishr and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, and Suleiman Ibn Yasar and Ata’, they said: If he is killed in the Sacred City, then one and a third of the blood money, and if he is killed in the Sacred Month, then Muharram pays heavy ransom."
"28184","(28184) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Ata’, Sa’id bin Jubayr, and Mujaid; They said: For the one who is killed in the Sanctuary, there is a blood money and a third of the blood money. And one of them said, I think it is. He said: Sa`id bin Jubayr: And whoever is killed in the Sanctuary pays a blood money and a third of the blood money."
"28185","(28185) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; He said: For a man who is killed in the Sacred Mosque, or during the months of the Sacred Mosque, a blood money and a third of the blood money."
"28186","(28186) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The blood money of one who is killed in the Sacred Mosque. And anything other than the sanctuary is the same."
"28187","(28187) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: I gave them both the same way."
"28188","(28188) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sa’id bin Abi Ma’shar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If he is killed in the Sacred Land In other than the Sacred Land, the blood money is one."
"28189","(28189) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hassan, he said: There is no more than a blood money. One, like Abraham said."
"28190","(28190) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: The blood money increases in the sacred month. And the forbidden, and the forbidden, and the neighbor."
"28191","(28191) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, he said: In the neighbor and in the sacred month there is severity."
"28192","(28192) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Amr bin Dinar and Suleiman Al-Ahwal informed me; Indeed, they heard a peacock saying: In the sanctuary, the sacred month, and the neighbor is harsh."
"28193","(28193) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The one who is killed in the Sacred Mosque does not exceed the amount of blood money he paid. He will be killed immediately."
"28194","(28194) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Samak bin Al-Fadl; That a man strangled a boy over his scarf, he said: So he wrote about it to Omar bin Abdul Aziz, and he wrote that he should be killed."
"28195","(28195) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: When he was strangled until He killed him, he was killed with him."
"28196","(28196) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: If a man strangles another, he does not raise his throat. On his behalf until he kills him, then it is a sacrifice, but if he abstains from it and then dies, his ransom is heavy."
"28197","(28197) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam; A man strangled another man and killed him, and blood money was imposed on him severely."
"28198","(28198) Abu Qutaybah and Abu Dawud al-Talisi told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Hammad, who said: It is a mistake."
"28199","(28199) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Harith; Concerning a man hitting another man, he said: If the witnesses testify that he hit him, then he did not stop sick from hitting him until he died. I obligated him to pay the blood money. If he was intentional, then the repayment. If it was a mistake, then the blood money is due on the wise."
"28200","(28200) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who strikes another man, and he continues to languish on his bed until he dies. He said: Concerning the punishment."
"28201","(28201) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Tamim bin Salamah, he said: Two men testified at a shard against a man. They said: We bear witness that this man struck this man, and he continued to squeeze him with his elbow until he died. Shurayh said: You bear witness that he killed him. ? They said: We bear witness that he killed him. He continued to squeeze him with his elbow until he died, so he said: Do you bear witness that he killed him?

(Abdul Razzaq 18300, Bayhaqi 134)"
"28202","(28202) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ibn Shihab told me; That Omar bin Al-Khattab had intercourse during his time with a man from Jehanna with a man from Banu Ghifar, or a man from Banu Ghifar with a man from He came to Jinnah, and his family claimed that he died from that. So Omar made fifty of the plaintiffs swear to them, but they refused to take the oath, and the defendant refused to take the oath. So Omar paid half the blood money on her. (Abdul Razzaq 18297. Malik 3)"
"28203","(28203) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Hassan bin Muslim informed me; A mother bit the finger of a servant of Banu Zayd, and it was buried in her and he died, so the maid confessed that she had bitten him. Then Omar ibn Abdul Aziz ruled that Banu Zayd should swear fifty oaths, and their oaths were repeated, as he died of She bit her, then the female slaves are theirs, otherwise they have no right, so they refused to swear an oath."
"28204","(28204) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Aoun, on the authority of Shuraih; That a man met a man with a chair and collided with him and killed him, so Shurayh said: The one who struck him was responsible for the one who was shocked."
"28205","(28205) Abdul Rahim bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ali; Two horsemen collided and one of them died, so the living was responsible for the dead."
"28206","(28206) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; He was asked about two ships that collided, and one of them sank? He said: The others are not liable, but whichever man anchors two ships on the way of the Muslims and they are hit, he is liable."
"28207","(28207) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali; Concerning the two knights clashing, he said: The living guarantees the blood money of the dead."
"28208","(28208) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ka’b bin Sur; A man was riding a donkey, and a man riding a camel met him in an alley. The donkey ran away, and the man was struck and something happened to him. Ka'b bin Sur, the owner of the camel, guaranteed something."
"28209","(28209) Shababi told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Muttalib bin Al-Sa’ib Al-Samimi, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab; Othman ruled that every two fighters fight each other for what is between them."
"28210","(28210) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a witness is directed at the owner of the leaning wall and he falls and is hit, He is a guarantor."
"28211","(28211) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Shuraih, he said: If the man’s wall Leaning and bearing witness to it, including it."
"28212","(28212) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Like him"
"28213","(28213) Abd al-Wahhab bin Ata’ al-Khaffaf narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders; He used to say in the Leaning Wall: If they testify against his companion and he kills a person, then he is liable."
"28214","(28214) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Aoun, on the authority of Shuraih; A boy jumped on another, and the lower one gave way and the folds of the upper one broke, so he secured the upper one, but did not secure the lower one."
"28215","(28215) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Imran bin Hudayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: If a man quarrels with another man and he dies One of them included the rest. He said: I said: Why? He said: Because the blood of a Muslim is not valid."
"28216","(28216) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; Two boys were playing tag, and one of them wrestled with the other, and one of them broke and the other’s folds broke, so he secured The highest is the lowest, and the lowest is not guaranteed by the highest."
"28217","(28217) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Shuraih; Concerning a man who fell on a man from the top of a house, and the one above him died. Shurayh said: I guarantee the land."
"28218","(28218) A partner narrated to us, he said: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: If the lowest dies among the highest,"
"28219","(28219) Abdul Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, who said: It was Two boys were playing, and one of them jumped on the back of his friend, and the folds of the upper part broke, and the lower part became severed, so he secured each other."
"28220","(28220) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hikam; Concerning a man who fell on top of a man on top of a house, and one of them died. He said: The living of the two of them is liable."
"28221","(28221) Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who jumped on another man, and the collar of the jumper broke and the one who was jumped was injured, so the collar of the jumper broke, and he was liable for it. He encouraged the one who was blamed."
"28222","(28222) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata’ told me, he said: Safwan bin Ya’la bin told me Umayyah, on the authority of his father, he said: I had a worker, and he fought a man, and one of them bit the other’s hand. Ata’ said: They informed me. Safwan, whoever bit the other, then the one who bitten took his hand from the biter’s mouth, and he took out one of his folds, so they came to the Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he neglected his second. (Bukhari 6893 and Muslim 1301)"
"28223","(28223) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Zurara, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, he said: So he delayed it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Bukhari 6892. Tabarani 533)"
"28224","(28224) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata’; That a man bit the hand of another during the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he pulled out his fold, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, threw it away. May God bless him and grant him peace."
"28225","(28225) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; He said: I was informed that a man bit another man’s hand, so he tore his hand from his mouth and dropped one or two folds from his mouth. So he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, begging, and he said to him: Would he put his hand in your mouth so that you could eat it? If you wish, you can push your hand towards him and he may bite it, then pull it away. (Muslim 1301, Ahmad 435)"
"28226","(28226) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, he said: Ibn Abi Mulki told me, on the authority of his grandfather; That a person came to Abu Bakr, and a person bit him and took his hand from him, and his folds went away, so Abu Bakr said: I have gone away. His folds"
"28227","(28227) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj; Abu Bakr and Omar invalidated it."
"28228","(28228) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Shuraih; Concerning a man who bit another man and his hand was torn off, and his folds were torn out, and a slice invalidated it."
"28229","(28229) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed; Two Bedouin men quarreled in Medina during the time of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, and one of them said to his friend: I hit him. By God, he even armed himself and said: Bear witness. By God, he spoke the truth, so Omar bin Abdul Aziz sent for Saeed bin Al-Musayyab. He asks him about a man who hit another man until he was armed. Is there a matter of the past or a Sunnah regarding that? Saeed said: Othman decided on it for a third of the blood money."
"28230","(28230) Ali bin Musir told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; Concerning a man, if he sustains wounds and retaliates for them and dies, he said: “His first wounds” are paid from the blood money of the dead person. Abdullah bin Dhakwan said: He does not have anything as a blood money for the dead."
"28231","(28231) Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He will be healed according to the extent of wounds."
"28232","(28232) Abduh bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: He will be relieved of his wounds, and he will be a guarantor for the rest of the blood money."
"28233","(28233) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: If the one against whom retaliation is being taken dies, then the retaliator is liable. To God."
"28234","(28234) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya; In Al-Muqtas: Which of the two of them died and was redeemed."
"28235","(28235) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: I asked Ziyad bin Jubayr for permission to perform Hajj, and he asked me about A man attacked another man and he retaliated against him, so the one who retaliated against him died? So I said: He must pay the blood money, and it will be removed from him according to the amount of grief. Then that matter came to pass, and Abraham came and I asked him? He said: The blood money is upon him."
"28236","(28236) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about that? They said: The blood money is due on him, and Hammad said: It will be removed from him according to the amount of grief."
"28237","(28237) Waki` narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, and al-Shu’abi, saying: Ali Blood money, and it will be removed from him according to the extent of grief."
"28238","(28238) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father (h) and on the authority of Ibn Juraij, Concerning Ataa, they said: He is obligated to pay blood money, and nothing will be taken away from him."
"28239","(28239) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ash`ath, on the authority of Amir (h) and on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Umair bin Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Khalas, on the authority of Ali; He said: Whoever dies in retaliation according to the Book of God, there is no religion for him."
"28240","(28240) Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Omar; Like him"
"28241","(28241) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who is punished and dies: he has no religion, the Book of God killed him."
"28242","(28242) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who dies in retaliation, he said: He has no blood money."
"28243","(28243) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of a sheikh from the people of Basra, on the authority of Abu Nadrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id; That Abu Bakr and Omar said: Whoever is killed by a Hadd has no reason."
"28244","(28244) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad; Concerning a man who is subjected to punishment and dies. They said: There is no blood money for him."
"28245","(28245) Abbad told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Umair bin Saeed, who said: Ali said: If a punishment is imposed on a man for adultery, or He stole from him, or slandered him and he died, so there is no compensation for him."
"28246","(28246) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar and Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Umair bin Sa’id al-Nakha’i, He said: Ali said: I would not impose a punishment on a man if he died and I would find in myself anything from him, except for the one who drinks alcohol, if he dies. And I paid tribute to him. Sufyan added: That is because the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not use it."
"28247","(28247) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair; Ali and Omar said: Whoever is killed by retaliation, there is no blood money for him."
"28248","(28248) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ali and Abdullah, who said: Intentional weapons."
"28249","(28249) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, similar to him."
"28250","(28250) Abu Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of the one who narrated to him, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: Baptism by needle, so what Above her"
"28251","(28251) Abbad told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, who said: The pillars are with iron."
"28252","(28252) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Everything is done with iron, so it is intentional."
"28253","(28253) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He is not driven by a striker, unless he strikes with an iron."
"28254","(28254) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Azib, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Everything is a mistake except the sword, and for every mistake there is an arrow."
"28255","(28255) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Intentional intent with a weapon."
"28256","(28256) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ziyad bin Al-Alaqah, on the authority of a man; A man threw a boulder at another man and killed him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, drove him away. (Bukhari 1903, Bayhaqi 43)"
"28257","(28257) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Striking a rock intentionally, and in it is the fuel."
"28258","(28258) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, who said: The man baptizes The most powerful, meaning strong, to the rock, or to the wood, and a man’s head is struck against it, and what pillar is more steadfast than this? ?"
"28259","(28259) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Jarwah ibn Hamil, on the authority of his father, who said: Omar said: He baptizes If one of you goes to his brother and hits him like a person eating meat, a man will not be brought to him who did that and was killed, but I will take him away from him."
"28260","(28260) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Should he hit him with a stick intentionally? If it kills its owner, the one who struck it will be killed."
"28261","(28261) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, who said: semi-intentional; With the stick and the great stone."
"28262","(28262) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Qais narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: If he was hit with a stick, he repeated it and started. He was killed"
"28263","(28263) Waki’ told us, he said: Shuabi told us, he said: I asked the arbitrator and Hammad about the man hitting the man with a stick. So he gets killed? The arbitrator said: There is no punishment for him, and Hammad said: He will be killed."
"28264","(28264) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: If he raises himself with a stick, then he is a force."
"28265","(28265) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas; A Jew crushed a woman’s head with a stone, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, crushed his head between two stones."
"28266","(28266) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; That a person was killed in Sana’a, and that Omar killed seven people there, and he said: If the people of Sana’a had rebelled against him, I would have killed them with him. All of you (Malik 871)"
"28267","(28267) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, who said: Omar said: If only he had joined The people of Sana'a will kill them."
"28268","(28268) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Omari told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; Omar bin Al-Khattab killed seven people of Sana’a with one man, and he said: If the people of Sana’a had participated in it, I would have killed them."
"28269","(28269) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Wahhab, he said: Men came out They were traveling and a man accompanied them. They came but he was not with them. He said: His family came to them, and Sharih said: Your witnesses are that they They killed your companion, otherwise they would swear to God that they would not kill him. So bring them to Ali while I am with him. He separated them and they confessed. So I heard Ali saying: I am Abu Al-Hasan Al-Qurm, so he ordered them to be killed."
"28270","(28270) Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard Suleiman ibn Musa, he said: There are people who give advice. All in the man, he will kill them all with him."
"28271","(28271) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: A man killed two free men intentionally? He said: This is what is used for food. (Abdul Razzaq 18087)"
"28272","(28272) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’abi; He killed seven people with one man."
"28273","(28273) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, who said, No. Two men are killed by one man."
"28274","(28274) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, who said: He was Abd al-Malik, and Ibn Al-Zubair will not be killed except one of them."
"28275","(28275) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: None of them will be killed except one."
"28276","(28276) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Hassan ibn Salih, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Dhul ibn Ka’b; That Muadh said to Omar: You do not have the right to kill two people with one life."
"28277","(28277) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, Abdullah bin Amr He said: A man was driving a donkey, and he was riding on it, and he hit it with a stick he had, and a splinter from it flew out and hit it. His eye, so I gouged it out. This was reported to Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, and he said: This is one of the hands of the Muslims. He did not hit it. An attack on someone, and he imposed a blood money on his wife."
"28278","(28278) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: A man injures himself by mistake. Is there a clear evidence on him? He said: You are wise, I am wise."
"28279","(28279) Harami bin Amara told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about two men who bore witness against another man. So his hand was cut off, so they looked and saw that one of the witnesses was a slave? They said: The Imam is guaranteed."
"28280","(28280) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: A man carried his son on a horse for Ashurah. So he poked him and attacked him and killed him, and made his blood money for his female relatives, and he did not leave anything to the father."
"28281","(28281) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: Did the man kill his son by mistake? He said: You are wise, I am wise."
"28282","(28282) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr bin Dinar informed me; On the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan, a man came to him who had killed his father and brother, and he said: There is your private property."
"28283","(28283) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Qaqa’, who said: I invited a people to my house and they ate food. And they drank, and became drunk, and went to the knives of the house, and struck with them, and they wounded one another, and there were four of them, and two died. Two of them remained, so Ali paid the blood money to all four of them, and recounted to the wounded the wounds that had befallen them."
"28284","(28284) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Zakaria narrated to us, on the authority of Amer; Al-Hasan bin Ali brought two men who killed three, and the two men were wounded. Al-Hasan bin Ali said: There is a debt on the two men. The three, and the wounds of the two men will be removed from them."
"28285","(28285) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, and Ibn Abi Malika, who said: If a man had killed A man, and the murdered man wounded the murderer, the murderer was killed, and the murdered person’s family took care of the murderer’s wound."
"28286","(28286) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: In a house, murder and quarrels were found, so he was made each other."
"28287","(28287) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: A group of people from Zurara came out and fought, and some of them were killed. Sometimes, Ali guaranteed the blood money of the slain, and made amends for the wounded in proportion to their wounds."
"28288","(28288) Muhammad ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If the dog was in the house, the people of the city called for prayer. The house belongs to the man, so he enters and occupies it, they are liable, but if he enters without permission and occupies it, they are not liable."
"28289","(28289) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Zakaria narrated to us, on the authority of Amir, who said: If their dog licked a span of an inch outside of their house, then Above him they are guaranteed."
"28290","(28290) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Qais narrated to us, he heard it from Al-Sha’bi, he said, When a man enters another man’s house, He is a guarantee until he brings it out as he entered it."
"28291","(28291) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: When he entered With their permission and he is destroyed, they are guaranteed, but if he enters without their permission and he is destroyed, they are not responsible."
"28292","(28292) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Tariq bin Abdul Rahman, he said: I was with Shurayh, and a questioner came to him. His sock was torn and his leg was scratched, so he said: I entered a people’s house and their dog bit me. Shurayh said: If they gave you permission They are guarantors, otherwise there is no guarantee on them."
"28293","(28293) Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hikam; Concerning the vengeful dog, he said: He is not liable."
"28294","(28294) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Amir, who said: He used to say about dogs when a man seduces them. And it is with the sheep and it becomes barren, then there is no liability for it, but if it encounters people on the road and harms someone, then there is liability for it."
"28295","(28295) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, and Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no force except by the sword."
"28296","(28296) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man killing a man with pebbles, or mutilating him with them. He said: “But killing with a sword” is not part of their matter."
"28297","(28297) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qais, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: There is no driving except with an iron."
"28298","(28298) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: There is no fuel except Ironically"
"28299","(28299) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Like him"
"28300","(28300) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a servant who commits crimes, he said: It will be given to them, and they divide it according to the amount of the crimes."
"28301","(28301) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Malik, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; Concerning a servant who made an accusation against a man, then made an accusation against another man, then made an accusation against another man, and he judged it for the last."
"28302","(28302) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hammad and Rabi’a, who said: They divide it according to shares."
"28303","(28303) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Kardam; That a man asked Ibn Abbas, Abu Hurairah, and Ibn Umar about a man who killed a believer. Is there any way he can repent? So they all said: Can he revive him? Can he create a tunnel on earth, or a ladder in the heavens? Can he not die?"
"28304","(28304) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abu Nasr, and Yahya al-Jabir, on the authority of Salem bin Abi al-Ja’d, on the authority of Ibn Abbas He said: A man came to him and said: O Abu Abbas, have you seen a man killed intentionally? What is his reward? He said: {His recompense is Hell to abide therein, and the wrath of God be upon him}. He said: What do you think if he repents, believes, and does righteous deeds? Then he converted? He said: How can he repent? Is your mother bereaved of you? On the Day of Resurrection, he will come holding his head, his cheeks extended, until he stands with it at the Throne, and he will say: Oh Lord, ask this why they killed me. (Tirmidhi 3029. Ahmad 222)"
"28305","(28305) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu al-Sufar, on the authority of Najiya, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The two things that are ambiguous are: polytheism and murder."
"28306","(28306) Waki’ told us, he said: Harith bin Al-Sa’ib told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: I have never quarreled with my Lord about anything. I have never quarreled with Him about the killer of a believer, and He has not answered me."
"28307","(28307) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Harun bin Saad, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, he said: I was with Ibn Umar in Fustatah, then a man asked him about a man who killed a believer intentionally? He said: Then Ibn Umar recited to him: {And whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell to abide therein} the verses, so look who She killed you"
"28308","(28308) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Salma bin Nubait narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: The one who kills a believer has no repentance."
"28309","(28309) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Abu Musa said: There is no adversary on the Day of Resurrection whom I hate A man whom I killed came to me, his cheeks were brimming with blood, and he said: O Lord, ask this why they killed me?"
"28310","(28310) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Salma bin Nubait narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Muzahim, who said: Because I repent from polytheism, I love I have to repent for killing a believer."
"28311","(28311) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Salama bin Nubait narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak; (And whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell to abide therein) He said: Nothing has abrogated it since it was revealed."
"28312","(28312) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Aidh, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir al-Janni, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever meets God, not associating anything with Him, does not regret the blood of a forbidden person. Heaven

(Ibn Majah 2418, Hakim 351)"
"28313","(28313) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah said: The man continues in the open spaces of His religion is as long as his hand is clean of blood, so if he dips his hand in unlawful blood, his life is removed."
"28314","(28314) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shimr, on the authority of Shar bin Hawshab, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, he said: He will come. The person who was killed on the Day of Resurrection will sit on the avenue, and when the killer passes by him, he will stand up to him and take his robe. So he says: O Lord, ask this man why he killed me? He said: Then he says: So-and-so commanded me. He said: Then the killer and the commander will be taken and thrown into the Fire."
"28315","(28315) Waki’ told us, he said: Abu Al-Ashhab told us, he said: I heard Mazahim Al-Dhabi talking to Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said While a man was drinking water in his cistern, and was waiting for a wolf to come to him, when a man riding, thirsty and reassured, came to him. He said: I want? He said: No. He said: So he stepped aside and mounted his mount. When it saw the water, it approached the basin and burst the basin. He said: Then the owner of the basin stood up. So he took a sword from his neck, then struck him with it until he killed him. He said: So he went out to ask for a fatwa, and he asked some of Muhammad’s companions. I am not He named them, and they all followed him, until one of them came and said: Can you produce it as you have mentioned? He said: No. He said: Can you seek a tunnel in the earth, or a ladder in the heavens? He said: No. He said: So the man got up and left for a short while. He called him and he returned him and said: Do you have any parents? He said: Yes, my mother is alive. He said: Carry her and honor her. If the other one enters the Fire, then God will keep away those who keep him away."
"28316","(28316) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Salam bin Miskin narrated to us, saying: Sulayman bin Ali narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri said: It was said to him in these verses: {Whoever kills a soul for other than manslaughter, or for corruption in the land, it is as if He killed all of the people. Is it for us what it was for the Children of Israel? He said: So he said: Yes, and there is no god but Him."
"28317","(28317) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: To the killer of the believer. Repent"
"28318","(28318) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: It was said: The killer repents when Regret"
"28319","(28319) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, he said: I do not know who killed The believer must repent, except for seeking forgiveness."
"28320","(28320) Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sabah bin Thabit, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: The killer has repentance."
"28321","(28321) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: A man came to Omar and said: I was killed, so what is the matter for me? Who repented? He said: Yes, so do not despair, and he recited to him from the protector of the believer: {Forgiver of sins and accepter of repentance, severe in punishment}"
"28322","(28322) Ibn Saeed told us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majliz; {So his reward is Hell}. He said: This is his reward, so if he wants to bypass his reward, he can do so."
"28323","(28323) Amr bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Sayyar, on the authority of Abu Salih; Like it"
"28324","(28324) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ziyad bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Ibn Maqil, who said to him: Did you hear your father say: I heard Abdullah say: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Repentance is regret? He said: Yes.

(Ibn Majah 4252. Ahmad 376)"
"28325","(28325) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ziyad bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Abdullah bin Maqil; That his father Maqil bin Muqrin Al-Muzani said to Ibn Masoud: Did you hear the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Repentance is regret? He said: Yes. (Ahmed 433)"
"28326","(28326) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i informed us, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, he said: He came A man went to Ibn Abbas and said: Does anyone who kills a believer repent? He said: No, except Hell. When he went, those sitting with him said to him: This is not how you used to give us fatwas. You used to give us fatwas that for whoever kills a believer Your repentance is accepted, so what is the matter today? He said: I think he is an angry man who wants to kill a believer. He said: So they sent for him and found him like that."
"28327","(28327) Abd bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He looked at the Ka'b and said: How great is your sanctity, and how great is your right, and the Muslim has a greater sanctity than you, may God sanctify him. His property, his blood is forbidden, his honor is forbidden, his harm is forbidden, and that he harbors an evil opinion of him."
"28328","(28328) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, He said: Killing a believer is greater in the sight of God than the disappearance of this world. (Tirmidhi 1395. An-Nasa’i 3449)"
"28329","(28329) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; {It is as if he had killed all of mankind}, he said: who spared it, {and whoever saves it, it is as if he had saved all of mankind}, he said: who is sufficient About killing her."
"28330","(28330) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid; {And whoever revives her}, he said: Whoever saves her from drowning or burning has revived her."
"28331","(28331) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Ala’ ibn Abd al-Karim narrated to us, saying: I heard Mujahid saying: {And who He brought her to life, and it was as if he had saved all mankind. He said: Whoever refrains from killing her has saved her."
"28332","(28332) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Miqdam, on the authority of Hubba bin Juwayn al-Hadrami, on the authority of Ali; {Our Lord, show us those who led us astray of the jinn and mankind}, the son of Adam who killed his brother, and Satan the demons."
"28333","(28333) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Malik bin Husayn, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Ali, said: The son of Adam who killed his brother and Satan."
"28334","(28334) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murra, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: No soul is killed unjustly, except that the first son of Adam owes a handful of its blood, because he was the first to The age of killing (Bukhari 6867. Muslim 27)"
"28335","(28335) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Hasan bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: What No soul is killed unjustly, but it is upon the first son of Adam, and Satan is a guarantor against it."
"28336","(28336) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid; {Corruption has appeared on land and sea because of what the hands of people have earned}. He said: On land is the son of Adam who killed his brother, and on the sea. The one who used to take every ship by force."
"28337","(28337) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hashim told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Whoever kills two men is a tyrant, and recited: “Do you want to kill me as you killed a soul yesterday? If you only want to be A mighty one."
"28338","(28338) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Whatever was killed with a weapon intentionally, then it is a punishment."
"28339","(28339) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Ali said: The pillars are all fuel."
"28340","(28340) Abdul Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Amir, Al-Hasan, Ibn Sirin, and Amr bin Dinar, they said: The pillars drive"
"28341","(28341) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Intentionality is an act of impunity, unless the guardian of the murdered person pardons him. (Abu Dawud 4527. An-Nasa’i 6992)"
"28342","(28342) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, Al-Hakam, and Hammad. They said: He did not hit him with a whip. Or a stick, or a stone, and it is less than the soul, so it is a pillar, and in it is fuel."
"28343","(28343) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If a man and a boy come together to kill a man, the man is killed. And upon the sane boy is the full blood money."
"28344","(28344) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, who said: Hammad was asked about a man and a boy who killed a man. Intentionally? He said: As for the man, he will be killed, and as for the boy, his guardians will pay his share of the blood money."
"28345","(28345) Muhammad bin Sawa’i told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he is helped by someone who cannot be guided by him, This is a religion."
"28346","(28346) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a boy and a slave come together to kill, then the blood money is paid. They gathered together, and he struck this man with a sword and this man with a staff, and he was killed."
"28347","(28347) Zaid told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Among the people they kill intentionally, and among them are the child and the imbecile. He said, “This is a blood money that is wrong for the sane woman.”"
"28348","(28348) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hassan, they said about a man who was killed intentionally, so the killer was imprisoned to bring him to justice. Then a man came and killed the killer by mistake, so they said: I will pay his ransom to his family. The imprisoned person, and Ataa said: For the family of the first killed person."
"28349","(28349) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The blood money is for the family of the murdered person."
"28350","(28350) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hammad, similar to what Al-Hasan said."
"28351","(28351) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who was killed while he had a small child. He said: That goes to his friends."
"28352","(28352) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, who said: I heard Hammad saying about a man who was killed, and some His guardians are young. He said: He kills his great guardians if they want, and they do not wait."
"28353","(28353) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hussein, on the authority of Zaid, on the authority of some of his family; Al-Hasan bin Ali killed Ibn Muljim, who killed Ali, and he had a young son."
"28354","(28354) Qubaisa narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: He will be kept safe until They grow up."
"28355","(28355) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, on the authority of Nafi’ ibn Abd al-Harith, he said: I wrote To Omar, may I ask him about a man who broke one of his elbows? So Omar wrote to me: There are two rights in it, two virgins."
"28356","(28356) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Salim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, who said: In the forearms, The two zindans are fifty dinars."
"28357","(28357) Sharik told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: A wounded person should not be retaliated until his wounds are healed."
"28358","(28358) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A wounder should not be retaliated until the one who caused the wound is healed."
"28359","(28359) Muhammad ibn Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: By using the fuel, one should wait for its owner to recover."
"28360","(28360) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Jabir; That a man stabbed a man in the knee with a horn, so he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, begging him, and it was said to him: Even He cleared his throat, but he refused and hastened and took his place. He said: Then his foot became stubborn and the man of the one being led was healed, so he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him and said: You have nothing, refuse.

(Daraqutni 89. Ahmed 217)"
"28361","(28361) Waki’ told us, he said: Shuabi told us, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about the man. The command of the man to kill the man? They said: The killer shall be killed, and there is no force on the one who commands it."
"28362","(28362) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer; About a man who ordered his servant to kill a man intentionally? He said: The slave will be killed."
"28363","(28363) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ali bin Salih, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who commands another man and he kills. He said: They are not partners.

 Waki` said: This is with us in the sin, so as for the punishment, it is only on the killer."
"28364","(28364) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, who said: I asked Ibrahim about a prince who commanded a man and he was killed. A man? He said: They are both partners in sin."
"28365","(28365) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Salama bin Nubait narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Muzahim; The authority orders a man to kill another man? Al-Dahhak said: Be the one who was killed."
"28366","(28366) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who commands his servant to kill the man? He said: The man will be killed."
"28367","(28367) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salama, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Khalas, on the authority of Ali; About a man who ordered his servant to kill a man? He said: It is like a whip or a sword."
"28368","(28368) Omar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; Concerning a man who orders his servant to kill a man. He said: He kills the master."
"28369","(28369) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr; A man added a piece of tail, and one of their maids went to cut firewood, so he wanted it to kill herself, so she chopped it up. With a camel and I killed him. Then it was brought to Omar Ibn Al-Khattab and he said: This is the one who has been killed by God. He will never die."
"28370","(28370) Hafs told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yusuf, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid; That a man wanted a woman to kill herself, so she raised a stone and killed him. This was reported to Omar, and he said: That is the one who is killed by God."
"28371","(28371) Aidh bin Habib told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar; A woman in the Levant came to Al-Dahhak ibn Qays and mentioned to him that a person had opened his door for her, and that she had sought help. No one helped her, and it was winter, so she opened the door for him, took a millstone, and threw it at him, killing him. So he sent with it. And behold, there was a thief among the thieves, and behold, there was with him some goods, and his blood was voided."
"28372","(28372) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided May the peace and blessings of God be upon him regarding a man who captured a man and was killed by another, that the killer should be killed, and the one who captured him should be imprisoned. (Daraqutni 140, Bayhaqi 50)"
"28373","(28373) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Ali; He ruled that the killer be killed, and that the one who caught him be imprisoned. (Abdul Razzaq 18089)"
"28374","(28374) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about the man who catches another man. And someone else kills him? They said: The killer will be killed."
"28375","(28375) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I heard Suleiman bin Musa say: The meeting among us is based on What is to be killed is that one man catches him, and the other strikes him. For with us they are partners in his blood. They will both be killed."
"28376","(28376) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir; That two men were brought to Ali, one of whom he killed, and the other captured him, so he killed the one he killed, and said to the one who captured him: I captured him to death. I will lock you up in prison until you die."
"28377","(28377) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib; Omar bin Abdul Aziz ordered that the Mudhahiyah be made clear."
"28378","(28378) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab He said: A rational person does not give anything, except a third and no more."
"28379","(28379) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Omar Ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sahimi, on the authority of a man; That a man came to Omar ibn al-Khattab for a clarification? He said: We do not negotiate between ourselves."
"28380","(28380) Waki’ told us, he said: Issa told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: There is no reason in anything other than the clarification."
"28381","(28381) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: When will the mind reach the level of being understood by the wise woman? All in all, if it reaches a third? He said: Yes, I think, and I have no doubt that he said: And unless it reaches a third, then the man’s people are responsible exclusively."
"28382","(28382) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mu’mil, he said: Omar bin Abdul Rahman Al-Samimi narrated to me, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Abi Rabah, on the authority of Abu Umayyah Al-Akhnas, said: I was sitting with Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, when a man from Banu Ghifar came and said: My son was upset and said: The people of the village cannot handle this chewing gum."
"28383","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Yunus told us, he said: Abu Abdul Rahman Baqi bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Abu Bakr told us, he said:

(28383) Abdul-A’la bin Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab; The Qasamah existed during the pre-Islamic period, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, approved it regarding a murdered Ansar who was found in A pocket for the Jews. He said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, started with the Jews and assigned them fifty shares. She said: The Jews: We will not swear. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to the Ansar: Will you swear? The Ansar refused to take the oath, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fined the Jews his blood money, because he was killed among them. Show them (Muslim 1295. An-Nasa’i 6911)"
"28384","(28384) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: Omar bin Abd al-Aziz called me and asked me about Al-Qasamah? He said: It seemed to me that I should return it. The Bedouin is testifying, and the absent man comes and testifies. So I said: O Prince. Believers, you will not be able to reject it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the caliphs after him have decided for it."
"28385","(28385) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders; That Suleiman bin Yassar narrated; Omar bin Abdulaziz said: I have never seen anything like an oath to be bound by it, and God says: {And call upon those who are just. Of you}, and the tribes said: {And We did not bear witness except to what we knew, and we were not guardians of the unseen}, and God said: {Except those who bear witness. In truth, and they know.

 Suleiman bin Yassar said: The division is true, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided for it, while the Ansar were with the Messenger of God. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when a man came out from among them. Then they went out from the presence of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and lo! Their companion was covered in his blood, so they returned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: The Jews killed us, and they called A man from among them, but they had no clear evidence, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them: Two witnesses besides you. Until he handed it over to you in its entirety, but they had no clear proof of it, so he said: Be entitled to fifty shares that I will hand over to you. In its entirety, they said: O Messenger of God, we hate to swear in the absence, so the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to He took the Jews' oath with fifty of them, and the Ansar said: O Messenger of God, the Jews do not care about swearing, Matthew We do not accept this from them. They came to us against the last of us, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeted him from his presence. (Bayhaqi 16371)"
"28386","(28386) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather; Huwaysiyya and Muhaysiyya, the sons of Masoud, and Abdullah and Abdul Rahman, the sons of so-and-so, went out to meet in Khaybar. Then he attacked Abdullah and was killed. He said: This was mentioned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He said: You swear by fifty and you are entitled to it. They said: O Messenger of God, how can we swear if we do not bear witness? He said: Then the Jews will absolve you, meaning, they will swear. He said: Then they said: O Messenger of God, when the Jews kill us. He said: So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, paid tribute to him from his presence.

(Ibn Majah 2678. An-Nasa’i 6922)

 (28386 AD) Abu Khaled said: Yahya bin Saeed told me, on the authority of Ibn Yasar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; Like this, except that he said: Abd al-Rahman, the brother of the murdered person, went speaking, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Pride, pride. He said: Then pride spoke, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You will swear by fifty oaths. Do you deserve it, or will it be divided to you by fifty? He said: They said: O Messenger of God, how do we accept the oaths of an infidel people? He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, paid tribute to him from his presence."
"28387","(28387) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Mas’udi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul-Rahman, he said: Two men from the people of Kufa to Omar bin Al-Khattab, and they found him leaving the House heading to Mina, so they circumambulated the House, then they reached him. So they told him their story, and said: O Commander of the Faithful, a cousin of ours was killed. We have a legal right to him in blood, and he... He was silent about them and did not return anything to them, until they called upon God and He burdened them, then God reminded him of them and He stopped them. Then Omar said: Woe to us if we are not reminded of God, and woe to us if we do not remember God. Among you are just witnesses. You will bring them upon the one who killed him, and we will spare you from it. Otherwise, he who will ward you off will swear by God: We have not killed, nor have we known a killer. If they eat, fifty of you will swear, and then the blood money is yours."
"28388","(28388) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq; A dead man was found in Banu Salul, so the saints came and cleared the name of Banu Salul, claimed another neighborhood, and brought a corpse. Bani Salul, so he asked them for clear evidence against the defendant."
"28389","(28389) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If a dead person is found alive Fifty men were taken from them, including the defendant, and if they were less than fifty, their oaths would be restored to them, the first then the first."
"28390","(28390) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Al-Azma’, he said: A person was found dead. In Yemen, he made clear, and he called upon him and welcomed him, so Amel Omar Ibn Al-Khattab wrote to him, and Omar wrote to him: Measure what is between. The two times, so to whichever was closer, take it. He said: So they measured it and found it closer to me. They called on it. He said: So he took us, fined us, and made us swear, so we said: O Commander of the Faithful, will you make us swear and fine us? He said: Yes, he said: Then fifty of us swore to God that I had not done it, nor did I know of a killer."
"28391","(28391) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; That a dead person was found in Yemen between two times. He said: Then Omar said: Look for the two living people closest to him, and take an oath from among them. Fifty men, by God, whom we have not killed, nor do we know of a killer, then the blood money will be upon them."
"28392","(28392) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar; Al-Zuhri was asked about a dead person who was found in a man’s house, and the owner of the house said: He knocked on me to rob me, so I killed him, and the family of The murdered man: He called him to his house and killed him. He said: Fifty of the murdered man’s family swore that he called him and killed him. It was limited to it, and if they eat it, they will pay a fine for the blood money. Al-Zuhri said: Ibn Affan made a ruling regarding a person killed from Banu Baqir Abi. His guardians were to take an oath, so Othman fined them the blood money."
"28393","(28393) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning the murdered person, a thief will be taken. He said: Fifty of the defendants will swear an oath: We did not kill, nor did we know about it. A murderer, then if they swear, they will be acquitted, but if they eat, fifty of the plaintiffs swear: Indeed, our blood will be shed before you, and then it will be paid."
"28394","(28394) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father; Concerning the Qasamah: It was still practiced during the pre-Islamic era and Islam."
"28395","(28395) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Ubaid, on the authority of Bashir bin Yasar; He claimed that a man from the Ansar called Saul bin Abi Hathama told him: A group of his people went to Khaybar and dispersed there, and they found one of them dead, so they said to those they found: They said: You killed our companion. They said: We did not kill him, nor did we know. So they went to the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said: O Prophet of God, we set out for Khaybar and found one of us killed. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Arrogance. He was arrogant, so he said to them: You will bring proof against whoever was killed. They said: We have no proof. He said: Then they will swear to you. They said: No. We were satisfied with the faith of the Jews, so the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided to stop his blood, so he ransomed him with a hundred The camels of charity"
"28396","(28396) Shababah bin Siwar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ruled that the oath is on the defendant. (Bukhari 6898)"
"28397","(28397) Muhammad ibn Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar informed me that he heard companions of theirs. They talk; Omar bin Abdul Aziz initiated the defendant’s oath, then Al-Aql included them."
"28398","(28398) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Muti’, on the authority of Fudayl ibn Amr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He has issued a ruling on the defendants."
"28399","(28399) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab; He saw the punishment on the defendants."
"28400","(28400) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, issued a ruling on the defendant."
"28401","(28401) Muhammad ibn Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ibn Shihab: Is the division in blood based on knowledge, or on knowledge? At all? He said: Absolutely."
"28402","(28402) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shuraih; He said regarding the division: I make them guilty and I know, meaning I make them swear: We did not kill, nor did we know of a killer."
"28403","(28403) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of al-Hasan ibn Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Every man among them shall take an oath. By God: I did not kill, nor did I know of a killer, then he would destroy him."
"28404","(28404) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: A person was found dead in Yemen in Wadi’ah. So it was brought to Omar, and he made them swear by fifty: We did not kill, nor did we know of a killer. Then he paid him his respects."
"28405","(28405) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He swears an oath to God: He did not kill us, nor We knew a killer."
"28406","(28406) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad; Indeed, Shurayh made them swear to God: We did not kill, nor did we know of a killer."
"28407","(28407) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika; Omar bin Abdul Aziz and Ibn Al-Zubair led the division."
"28408","(28408) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zahri; He used to say: “Qasamah is judged by it.”"
"28409","(28409) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Mas’udi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qasim, he said: Omar said: Al-Qasamah only necessitates reason, and it does not It stimulates the blood."
"28410","(28410) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of al-Hasan; That Abu Bakr, Omar, and the first group did not kill by force."
"28411","(28411) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of al-Hasan ibn Amr, on the authority of Fudail, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Reward by oath. Injustice"
"28412","(28412) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, he said: The Qassamah are worthy of the blood money, but no He is led by it."
"28413","(28413) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Saeed narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma’shar narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Nakha’i, he said: Al-Qasama. He is entitled to blood money for it, but he cannot be punished for it."
"28414","(28414) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: No one will be killed by division except one."
"28415","(28415) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Abi Uthman, he said: Abu Raja’, the client of Abi Qalab, narrated to me, on the authority of Abi Qalaba Omar bin Abdulaziz revealed his bed to the people one day, then he gave them permission and they entered upon him, and he said: What do you say about it? Al-Qasamah? So the people became angry and said: We say that retribution is right, and the Caliphs have led by it. (Bukhari 6899. Abu Dawud 273)"
"28416","(28416) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There are two witnesses besides you. (Abu Dawud 4513)"
"28417","(28417) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Mas’udi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qasim, he said: Two men from the people of Kufa set out for Omar bin Al-Khattab, and they found him had left the house, so they said: O Commander of the Faithful, a cousin of ours has been killed, and we have an equal treaty with him. In the blood, and he was silent about them, he said: Two just witnesses that you will bring against whoever killed him, so we will rescue you from it."
"28418","(28418) Abd al-Rahim told us, on the authority of al-Hasan ibn Amr, on the authority of Fudail, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Two witnesses to bloodshed."
"28419","(28419) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It is not permissible to drive except four witnesses."
"28420","(28420) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Two witnesses."
"28421","(28421) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If the portion does not reach, Repeat until they take fifty oaths."
"28422","(28422) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: An oath came, but they did not fulfill it. Fifty, and he returned the portion to them until they had fulfilled it."
"28423","(28423) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shuraih, he said: If they were Less than fifty, the oaths were repeated to them."
"28424","(28424) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid al-Hudhali, on the authority of Abu Malih; Omar bin Al-Khattab repeated his faith to them."
"28425","(28425) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If they were less than fifty The faith was repeated to them, the first and the first."
"28426","(28426) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz; He repeated the oaths to seven people in the Qasamah, one of them was an uncle."
"28427","(28427) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If a man is less than fifty in the share, he will not We accomplished it."
"28428","(28428) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, who said: As for what people are facing today, it is repeating. Faith"
"28429","(28429) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ja`far; When Ali found the murdered person between the two villages, he measured what was between them."
"28430","(28430) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: A person was killed between two times from Hamdan, between He called him and Khiwan, so he sent with them Omar al-Mughirah ibn Shu`bah, and said: Go with them and trace what is between the two villages. Whichever of them is closer, the one killed will join them."
"28431","(28431) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Al-Azma’, he said: A person was found dead. In Yemen, he made clear, and he supplicated and welcomed, so Amil Omar wrote to him, so Omar wrote to him: Measure what is between the two times. So whichever is closer, take it."
"28432","(28432) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Ishaq, who said: I heard Salim bin Abdullah, saying: And he A group of people from Banu Layth were able to take an oath tomorrow regarding the oath, so he said: O servants of God, there are people who swear to something that they did not They narrated it, but they did not attend it, nor did they witness it. And if I, or me, had anything to do with the matter, I would have punished them, or I would have slandered them, or I would have made them a punishment, and I would not have accepted from them any testimony."
"28433","(28433) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Abi Uthman, he said: Abu Raja’i, the client of Abu Qalab, narrated to me, on the authority of Abi Qalaba Omar bin Abdulaziz revealed his bed to the people one day, then he gave them permission and they entered upon him, and he said: What do you say about it? Al-Qasamah? So the people became angry, and they said: We say: Al-Qasamah is a right to lead with, and the Caliphs have led with it, so he said: What do you say, Abu Qalab? And he appointed me as a appointee for the people. I said: O Commander of the Faithful, you have the nobles of the Arabs and the heads of the soldiers. Have you seen that if there were fifty? Some of them testified against a man in Hummus that he had stolen, but they did not see him. Would you cut him off? He said: No, I said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, never killed anyone, except in one of three cases: A man who kills Through his own crime, or a man who committed adultery after being married to him, or a man who waged war against God and His Messenger and apostatized from Islam."
"28434","(28434) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla told us, on the authority of Ata’; The people were evacuated from a person killed during the Tawaf, so he was paid a ransom from the Bayt al-Mal."
"28435","(28435) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Wahb ibn Uqba and Muslim ibn Yazīd ibn Mathkur narrated to us, they heard him from Yazid bin Mathkur; People crowded into the Grand Mosque in Kufa on Friday, so they released a dead man, and Ali bin Ubayy paid him his ransom. A student from the treasury."
"28436","(28436) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Shu`ba narrated to us, on the authority of al-Hikam, on the authority of Abraham; That a man was killed while circumambulating, so he consulted the people’s age, and he said to Ali: I will pay his ransom to the Muslims, or in the treasury."
"28437","(28437) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: A falling stone came at the command of Marwan, and it hit Ibn Nastas bin Amer bin Abdullah bin Nastas, it is not known who his companion was, so he killed him, so Marwan struck his death on the people."
"28438","(28438) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a people who fought each other, and they injured a man, and it is not known which of them injured him. He said: The blood money is upon them all."
"28439","(28439) Ibn Ulayya told us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawwi, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He will pay back rewards according to the amount of money he has freed from him, and according to the amount What was lost on him was the slave’s blood money.

(Abu Dawud 457. Ahmed 260)"
"28440","(28440) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Ali said: He is one of the offices. As much as he did."
"28441","(28441) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham Al-Dastawai, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir; Ali and Marwan used to say in their letters: “The blood money of a freed man shall be paid in proportion to what he paid, and whatever small amount of blood money he has made.” The slave"
"28442","(28442) Muhammad bin Sawa’i told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: Office surgeon Abd surgeon"
"28443","(28443) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: His wounds cost him the reward of what he performed."
"28444","(28444) Muhammad bin Sawa’i told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Mansour, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: His wounds The offices are Abdul's wounds."
"28445","(28445) Waki` told us, on the authority of Shu`bah, he said: I asked al-Hakam and Hammad about a man who threw fire into a people’s house and they were burned? They said: There is no punishment for him, he cannot be killed."
"28446","(28446) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Husayn, on the authority of Yahya bin Yahya al-Ghassani, who said: A man burned straw in his sores, and sparks of fire came out, until it burned something for his neighbour. He said: So I wrote in it: Omar bin Abdul Aziz, so he wrote to me: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The foreigners are tyrannical, and I see that the Fire Mighty

(Abu Dawud 4582, Ibn Majah 2676)"
"28447","(28447) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a man who burned down a house, so he burned it. People? They said: He shall not be killed."
"28448","(28448) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: Makhoul narrated to me, he said: When Omar Bayt came before us Al-Maqdis gave Ubadah ibn al-Samit a man from among the non-Muslims to hold his animal, but he refused, so he encouraged him, explaining. Then he entered the mosque, and when Omar came out, the Nabati shouted to Omar, and Omar said: Who is the owner of this? His servants said: I am the owner of this. He said: What did you want for this? He said: I gave him my animal so he could handle it, but he refused, and I was a man in a state. He said: Either not, so sit down to drive. He said to him: Zayd ibn Thabit: You would not restrain your servant from your brother. He said: By God, if I refrain from driving you, I will help you. In the matter of blood money, give him her mind twice."
"28449","(28449) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: There is no force between a Christian and a free man. A Muslim, nor between a Christian and a Muslim servant."
"28450","(28450) Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khaled Al-Naili, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad; They said about a man who stabbed another man and his eye went away. The arbitrator said: If they bear witness that it went away from the blow, then it is It is permissible, and Hammad said: If they testify that he struck you on the day he struck you and it was true, then it is permissible."
"28451","(28451) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Hanash ibn Al-Mu’tamir, who said: I dug a hole in the right hand for the lion and it fell. There was a lion in it, so people started competing for the head of the well, and a man fell into it and clung to another, and the other clung to another. So four people were killed there and they were all destroyed, and the people did not know what to do. Then Ali came and said: If you wish. I have made a decision between you that will be permissible between you, until you come to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Then I will make The blood money is due on whoever is present at the head of the well, so he pays a quarter of the blood money to the first one who went into the well, and a third of the blood money to the second. The third was half the blood money, and the fourth was full. He said: So they agreed on that until they came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So they informed him of Ali’s judgement, so he allowed the judgement. (Ahmad 77. Tayalisi 114)"
"28452","(28452) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Habib bin Abi Thabit narrated to us, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Masruq; Six of his boys went swimming, and one of them drowned, and three testified that two of them drowned. And two testified against three that they drowned him, so Ali ruled that the three were to pay five-fifths of the blood money, and the two were to pay Three-fifths of the blood money."
"28453","(28453) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq; He made the blood money into weeks: four, divided by three, and three, divided by four."
"28454","(28454) Ibn Mushir told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Khalas, who said: A man hired four men to dig He had a well, so they dug it, and the well caved in on them, and one of them died, so that matter was reported to Ali, so he included the three. Quarters of the blood money, and a quarter of the blood money was subtracted from them."
"28455","(28455) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abu Malik narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Aqmar; That a man hired three people to dig a wall for him, so they all hit the roots of it, then he fell on them and one of them died. So they disputed into one party, and two-thirds of the blood money was awarded to the rest."
"28456","(28456) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; He was asked about workers who were hired to demolish a wall, and he fell down on them, and some of them died? He pays some fines to others, and the blood money is borne by whoever remains."
"28457","(28457) Waki’ told us, he said: Musa bin Ali told us, on the authority of his father, he said: A blind man came to seek the people during the time of Omar. He says:

O people, you have encountered an abomination. Can the blind, healthy, and seeing man understand?

 They both fell apart together?

 Waki` said: They saw that a healthy man was leading a blind man, so they fell into a well, and he fell on him, and either killed him. Or he injured him, then he took care of the blind man."
"28458","(28458) Abdi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; That a man from the people of the Levant was called: Ibn Khaybari. He found a man with his wife and he killed her, or he killed them, so he was brought to the court. Mu'awiyah, so it became difficult for him to decide on that matter, so he wrote to Abu Musa: Ask Ali about that, so he asked Abu Musa. Alia? He said: This is something happening on our land. I asked you to tell me, so he told him. Ali said: I am Abu Hassan. He did not bring four witnesses, so let them repel him entirely. (Abdul Razzaq 17915)"
"28459","(28459) Asbat narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Salama, who said: A man was brought to Mus’ab who found a man with his wife and killed him. So his blood was invalidated."
"28460","(28460) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Asim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: There were two brother men from the Ansar. It is said For one of them: Ash'ath, so he fought with one of the Muslim armies. He said: Then his brother's wife said to her brother: May you have Is your brother’s wife with a man to speak to her? So he went up and looked over her, and they were together on her bed, and she was plucking his chickens, and he said:

And I am more disheveled than Islam has become jealous of me

I spent the night on my tummy and in the evening

As if the places of the calves were

I was alone with his wedding all night long

On the blood of those who follow the belt

Fa'am has been combined into Fa'am

 He said: Then the man jumped to him and struck him with the sword until he killed him, then he threw him and he became killed in Medina, so Omar said: Sing. By God, there was a man who had this kind of knowledge, but he did it. Then the man got up and told him the story, so he said: It is crushed and went away."
"28461","(28461) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: A man finds a man with his wife. So he kills him, or sheds his blood? He said: There is no matter except with clear proof. I said: If it is testified that he committed adultery with his family, he said: And if it is testified, there is no matter but With the clear proof, there is no command except in the clear proof."
"28462","(28462) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamī, on the authority of Abd Allah, he said: We were among us during the night. In the mosque, a man came and said: If a man found another man with his wife and killed him, would you kill him? Did you flog him if he spoke? I would have mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He came to him, and he mentioned that to him, but she remained silent about him, and the verses were revealed. Cursing, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, called him and recited it to him. Then the man came after he had slandered his wife, and the Messenger of God cursed God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came between them, and said: Perhaps you will bring him black and curly. So she brought him black and curly. (Muslim 10. Abu Dawud 2247)"
"28463","(28463) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ward, on the authority of al-Mughirah, he said: The Prophet conveyed the message May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that Saad bin Ubadah said: If I had found a man with her, I would have struck him with an unarmored sword. He said: So he said The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Are you surprised by someone other than Saad? By God, I am more jealous than Saad, and God is more jealous than you, and because of God’s jealousy, God has forbidden indecency, whatever appears of it. And what they concealed."
"28464","(28464) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Mughirah ibn Al-Nu’man, on the authority of Hani’ ibn Hizam, in which Yahya added: Ibn Adam: On the authority of Malik Ibn Anas, on the authority of Hani Ibn Hazzam; That a man found a man with his wife and killed her, so he wrote about it to Omar, so Omar wrote about it two letters: a book about In public: he will be killed, and in secret: blood money will be taken."
"28465","(28465) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Al-Numan, on the authority of his mother; A woman from Banu Layth, called Umm Aaron, while she was sitting, was cutting some of the flesh of her sacrifice. A dog in the house was eating that meat, so she threw it with a knife and missed it, and her son objected to it, so the knives fell into it. His stomach was upset, so he died, and Ali from the treasury paid tribute to him."
"28466","(28466) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Khalas, who said: A man threw a stone at his mother and killed her, so he sought inheritance from his brothers, and his brothers said: You have no inheritance, so they went to Ali, so he removed him from the inheritance, and he decided Ali with the blood money, and he said: That stone protected you from it."
"28467","(28467) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid (h) and on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather (h) and on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Abu al-Malih (h) and on the authority of Ata’; That Qatadah had a son’s mother who was taking care of his sheep, and his son from her said to him: Until when will my mother be safe? By God, no. He asked her more than he asked her: Are you here? So he struck him with the sword and killed him, so Suraqah ibn Jasham wrote to Umar about that, and he wrote to him: “Let me die with him.” And for two hundred and forty, Hajjaj said: And some of them said: And for forty and a hundred, so he took thirty rights from it, and thirty A lump of money, and forty of them until the year of Basil, all of which he left behind, so he divided them among his brothers, and he did not He inherits something from him."
"28468","(28468) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Awf, he said: Omar bin Hayyan Al-Hamanani used to make horses, and he carried his son On a horse, it fell down and dripped from the horse and it died, so the blood money was imposed on its female relatives, for a time longer than sight."
"28469","(28469) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: A man carried his son on a horse to support him. So he poked him, and attacked him and killed him, so his blood money was determined by his female relatives, and he did not leave anything to the father."
"28470","(28470) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Khalas, on the authority of Ali; Two men came to Ali and bore witness that a man had stolen, so he cut off his hand. Then they brought another, and they said: This is him. He said: So he accused them of this, and he included this as the first."
"28471","(28471) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ibn Juraij told us, he said: Ammard told me; That Huyay ibn Ali told him, that he heard Ali tell him; That a man came to Ali and said to him: Fight this man. So Ali pushed him to him, so they stabbed him with their swords, until they saw They killed him and he died, so his family took him and treated him until he was healed. Then Ali came and said: Did I not repel him? To you? So he told him his news, so he called Ali, and found him paralyzed, so his wounds were treated, and they found blood on him, so he said to him: Ali: If you wish, pay him his blood money and kill him. Otherwise, let him go. He joined Umar and sought Ali, and Umar agreed. And Ali has the duty of Ali, whether he pays the blood money to him and he kills him, or he leaves him and he does not kill him, and Omar said To Ali: Indeed, you are a judge, then return him to his work."
"28472","(28472) Abbad and Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Omar, He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: The father should not be killed for the child. (Ibn Majah 2662. Daraqutni 181)"
"28473","(28473) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid and Ata, who said: A man should not be led by his parents, even if they kill him. Be patient"
"28474","(28474) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, who said: He wrote to Omar about a woman. She took a man's vagina, and it pierced the skin but did not pierce the peritoneum. Omar said to his companions: What do you think about this? They said: Make it in the same place as a jayfa. Omar said: But I think otherwise. I see that it contains half of what is in a jayfa."
"28475","(28475) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib; That a man forced a woman to leave her, so Omar struck him and fined him a third of her blood money."
"28476","(28476) Zaid bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Khaled bin Abdullah, on the authority of Khaled Al-Hadha’, on the authority of Aban bin Othman; A man who had married a female slave was brought to her, and he was pleased with her, and he and Omar bin Abdul Aziz said about her: If she was among those If he has intercourse with someone like her, then there is nothing on him, but if she is one of those who do not have intercourse like her, then he must pay a third of the blood money."
"28477","(28477) Waki’ told us, on the authority of a sheikh, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Zaid bin Thabit; Concerning a man who separates a woman, he said: If one of them keeps away from the other, then a third, and if he does not hold back, then the blood money."
"28478","(28478) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; A man took a drink at the door of some people, but they refused to give him something to drink, so he became thirsty and died, so Omar took care of them."
"28479","(28479) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: He was not killed during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. Neither Abu Bakr nor Omar is a man from among the Muslims unless he commits adultery, murder, or wars against God. And His Messenger."
"28480","(28480) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murra, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: It is not permissible to shed the blood of anyone who bears witness that there is no god but God, and that he is the Messenger of God, except one. Three people; A life for another, the married adulterer, the one who abandons his religion, the one who separates from the community. (Bukhari 6878, Muslim 1302)"
"28481","(28481) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Ghalib, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is not permissible to shed the blood of a Muslim, except for a man who killed and was killed, or a man who committed adultery after being married. Or a man who apostatized after his conversion to Islam. (Ahmad 2050, Tayalisi 1543)"
"28482","(28482) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Ghalib, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace; Like him"
"28483","(28483) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha said: The blood of none of the people of this tribe is not permissible, except for those who make three things permissible; The killing of a person by another person, the married adulterer, the one who separates from the Muslim community, or the one who leaves the Muslim community. (Hakim 354)"
"28484","(28484) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Qais narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn; Othman supervised the people on the day of the final, and said: Did you not know that it is not permissible to shed the blood of a Muslim except four times? A man who killed and was killed, or a man who committed adultery after being married, or a man who apostatized after his conversion to Islam, or a man who did the actions of the people of Lot. (Nasa’i 3520, Ahmad 63)"
"28485","(28485) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Aqmar, who said: I found a slave of ours who was working in... A well in the house of Utba, so I disputed with him to Sharih, and he said: I made it clear to you that they hated him, otherwise I will swear to you from his family. Home wherever you want."
"28486","(28486) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Shihab said to me: There is no share in the slave, and it should not be returned. By the price, the price is the same as the truth is claimed."
"28487","(28487) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Hisham bin Abdul-Malik ruled in the case of Abdul Ayyub, his client. Ibn Nafi’ made fifty oaths to Ayyub, so he swore and took the price for it."
"28488","(28488) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, who said: Salman said: As for the blood And his life will be spent in it."
"28489","(28489) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of al-Nazzal ibn Sabrah, he said: Omar wrote to the commanders of the soldiers: Not to be killed in inferiority to anyone."
"28490","(28490) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: He would not judge a bloodshed without the Commander of the Faithful."
"28491","(28491) Abdullah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; One of Hafsah’s maids witchcraft on her, and they found out about her witchcraft and she confessed to it, so she ordered Abd al-Rahman bin Zayd to kill her, and the news was reached. That was Uthman, but he denied it and became harsh against him, so Ibn Umar came to him and told him that she had bewitched him and confessed to him, and they found They bewitched her, and it was as if Othman only denied that because she was killed without his permission."
"28492","(28492) Hafs told us, he said: I asked Omar: What did Al-Hasan use to say in certain gatherings, “He should be killed?” He said: If they interact with each other, then it is the responsibility of the rational ones, and if they do not interact with each other, then a debt is owed in his wealth."
"28493","(28493) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; In times of covenant killing, he said: His death is for the Muslims and his reward is for them."
"28494","(28494) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders; Concerning a man from the people of Dhimma who gouged out the eye of a Muslim man and said: I will kill him on the people of Tassujah."
"28495","(28495) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Hammad; About four people who witnessed a man committing adultery and he was stoned, then one of them came back and said: He owes a quarter of the blood money."
"28496","(28496) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Ikrimah; About four people who testified against a man with a hadd punishment, then one of them lied to himself, saying: He will be fined a quarter of the blood money."
"28497","(28497) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He will be killed, and the blood money must be paid by the others."
"28498","(28498) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayoub Abi Al-Ala’, he said: Abu Hashim said; There were four people who testified against a man for adultery, then one of them came back and said that he owed a quarter of the blood money, and Ibn Sirin said: If he said I made a mistake and wanted someone else, so he must pay the full blood money, and if he says, “I intended to kill him,” he will be killed for it."
"28499","(28499) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: If the father grants the little girl who afflicts his son She passed it."
"28500","(28500) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid; Concerning a man whose hand was cut off during theft, then a man cut off his other hand afterward, saying: It contains half the blood money."
"28501","(28501) Shababah bin Siwar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a man who performed ablution and poured water into it. The way? Hammad said: He is guaranteed, and Al-Hakam said: He is not guaranteed."
"28502","(28502) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer; Concerning the butcher, and the butcher cleans his door, he said: He guarantees."
"28503","(28503) Abd al-Salam told us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of al-Hikam, and Hammad; Concerning a common man who sprinkles water at his door, and a person passes by him and slips and becomes distressed. Hammad said: He is sure, and he said Ruling: Not guaranteed."
"28504","(28504) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Awf, who said: I witnessed Abd al-Rahman bin Adhainni cutting off a man in Harisat. His head, then the avenger imprisoned him until the avenger saw him. He said: Ibn Sirin denounced this confinement."
"28505","(28505) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ata’ said: There is retaliation for wounds, but the imam does not have the right to retaliate. Beating him, not imprisoning him, is only retaliation. God has not forgotten. If He had willed, He would have ordered imprisonment and beatings."
"28506","(28506) Gandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Shebak, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hunay ibn Nuwayra, On the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The most chaste people are those who kill the people of faith.

(Abu Dawud 2459. Ibn Hibban 5994)"
"28507","(28507) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah; He passed by Ibn Muqabar, and Ziyad had cut off his hands and feet, and he said: I heard Abdullah say: The most chaste of people Killing the people of faith."
"28508","(28508) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abu Qalabab, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, who narrated it, and said: God has prescribed good deeds over all things, so when you kill, kill well. (Muslim 1549. Abu Dawud 2807)"
"28509","(28509) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Muslimah ibn Nawfal, on the authority of Safiyya bint al-Mughirah ibn Shu`bah, she said: No. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated the example. (Ahmed 246)"
"28510","(28510) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Shaddad ibn Aws, who narrated it, He said: God has ordained for you good deeds in everything, so when you kill, kill well, and if you slaughter, do well. Slaughter

(Muslim 1548, Bayhaqi 68)"
"28511","(28511) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Mas’udi narrated to us, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The most chaste people are the people of faith."
"28512","(28512) Abdul Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Bukair bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Ubaid bin Ta’la, He said: We invaded the land of the Romans, and with us was Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and over the people was Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid bin Al-Walid, in the time of Muawiyah. While we were with him, a man came to him and said: The prince was just brought with a cure. Four of them, so he ordered them to be patient, throwing arrows until they were killed. He said: Then Abu Ayyub stood up in fear until Abd al-Rahman came. He said: Have you been patient with them? I have heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbidding the patience of animals, and I do not like that you have been patient with chickens and that For such-and-such, he said: This is great, so Abdul-Rahman called for four of his servants and freed them in the place of what he had done."
"28513","(28513) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Adiy bin Thabit, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd, he said: He forbade. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated the example."
"28514","(28514) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Hiyaj bin Imran Al-Burjami, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn and Samurah bin Jundub said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the like.

(Abu Dawud 2460; Ahmad 429)"
"28515","(28515) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Hafs, on the authority of Ali ibn Murra, who said: I heard the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: God said: Do not imitate My servants. (Ahmad 1731. Tabarani 698)"
"28516","(28516) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Talq ibn Habib; In His saying: {So let him not be extravagant in killing}, He said: To kill someone other than your killer, or imitate your killer."
"28517","(28517) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khusayf, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr; {So let him not be extravagant in killing}, he said: to kill two with one."
"28518","(28518) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Alqamah ibn Marthad, on the authority of Sulaiman ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, he said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent a convoy, he would say: Do not imitate. (Muslim 1356. Abu Dawud 2605)"
"28519","(28519) Uqba bin Khalid Al-Sakouni told us, on the authority of Musa bin Muhammad bin Ibrahim, he said: My father told me, on the authority of my father Saeed said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the mutilation of animals."
"28520","(28520) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Rabi’i bin Othman Al-Taymi narrated to us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim; That Abu Musa wrote to Omar: The man will die before us and he has no kin or guardian. He said: So Omar wrote to him: If he leaves He who has a kinship, then the kinship, otherwise it is the loyalty, otherwise it is the treasury, they inherit it, and they are free from it."
"28521","(28521) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi (h) and Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who embraces Islam and has no master, they said: His inheritance is for the Muslims, and his inheritance is upon them."
"28522","(28522) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man submits to Islam at the hands of another man, he has his inheritance, and it is reasonable. about him"
"28523","(28523) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hakam ibn Al-Araj, on the authority of Al-Ash’ath ibn Thurmaliya, on the authority of Abu Bakra, he said : The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Whoever kills a person with a covenant with him other than what he has permissible, God forbids him to go to heaven. He smells its scent. (Hakim 8743. Ahmad 38)"
"28524","(28524) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Bakra, on the authority of the Prophet; Like him (Ahmed 52)"
"28525","(28525) Waki’ told us, he said: Uyaynah bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Bakra, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whoever kills a person with a covenant in a state other than that, God will forbid Paradise for him. (Abu Dawud 2754. Ahmad 38)"
"28526","(28526) Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Amr told us, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever kills a covenanter unjustly will not smell the scent of Paradise, and indeed he will be there. A fragrance from a journey of forty years. (Bukhari 3166; Ibn Majah 2686)"
"28527","(28527) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: The first thing that will be judged between people on the Day of Resurrection will be bloodshed. (Muslim 1304. Tirmidhi 1397)"
"28528","(28528) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Amr bin Shurahbil, he said: The first thing to be decided Among the people on the Day of Resurrection, there will be bloodshed. A man will come, taking another man by the hand. He will say: O Lord, this one killed me. He says: Why did you kill him? He will say: I killed him so that the honor would be for so-and-so. Then it will be said: It is not his. Do your deeds, and the man will come, taking him by the hand. The man, and he says: O Lord, this man killed me, and he says: Why did you kill him? So he says: I killed him so that you might gain honor. He said: So he says: Glory is mine. (Nasa’i 3460. Tabarani 10075)"
"28529","(28529) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Qais bin Abbad, who said: Ali said: I will be the first to kneel before the adversary before God on the Day of Resurrection. (Bukhari 4744)"
"28530","(28530) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Fudail bin Marzuq narrated to us, on the authority of Atiya bin Saad al-Awfi, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Jundub, on the authority of Ali; He was asked about those who killed him, and those who killed Muawiyah? He said: I and Mu'awiyah will come and we will dispute before the Throne. Wherever we are, there is a falaj, so its companions have entered a falaj."
"28531","(28531) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The first thing to be paid There will be bloodshed among the people on the Day of Resurrection."
"28532","(28532) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If a man sustains his wounds, retaliate against him. His companion, the blood money of the one who took revenge on him was on his sane person, the one who retaliates."
"28533","(28533) Abdul Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim; In the one who is retaliated against and dies, his wounds are absolved from the one whose blood retaliation is retaliated, and his blood money is due upon him. I have made up for it"
"28534","(28534) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; Concerning the one who is retaliated against and dies, he said: The blood money is due on his female relatives."
"28535","(28535) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning excess age, he said: government."
"28536","(28536) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: I narrated on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit; He said: The extra tooth is a third of a tooth."
"28537","(28537) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Mas’udi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abd al-Rahman, who said: A man approached his female slave from Al-Qadisiyah, he passed by a man standing on an animal, and the man poked the animal, so the animal raised its foot, and the eye did not miss The slave girl, so it was brought to Salman bin Rabi’ah Al-Balili, who included the passenger. This was reported to Ibn Masoud, and he said: Ali is the man. Only the puncher is guaranteed."
"28538","(28538) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, he said: I asked him about a man who was touched by a man’s animal? He said: The puncher is liable."
"28539","(28539) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: Unless someone pricks it, then the one who pierces it is liable."
"28540","(28540) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir (h) and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; They said about a man who cut off the whole nose of a servant. He said: He will be fined for his price."
"28541","(28541) Qubaisa bin Uqba narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Abu Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Concerning a man whose hand was cut off, so he made a settlement with her, then his hand was canceled and he died. He said: The settlement is rejected, and it is taken in exchange for the blood money."
"28542","(28542) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Trials raged and the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace, they are available, so their opinion is unanimous that he should not be led away, nor should he protect anyone who is correct about the interpretation of the Qur’an. What is correct in the interpretation of the Qur’an is not rejected, except what is found in its essence."
"28543","(28543) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I asked him about a boy who used to fly doves over a house. And a man was standing on top of a house, and the boy fell down, and Abraham said: Perhaps they will say, “Perhaps he has commanded something.”"
"28544","(28544) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Imran bin Hudayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: If you said to a man who is He was killed, which means his kingdom: a bridge, or a wall, far away from the fear of him, so pay off his fine."
"28545","(28545) Muhammad ibn Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: A man called out to a boy who was late, and he fell down and died? He said: They narrate on the authority of Ali that he fined him. They say: He frightened him. I said: So he called Kabir? He said: I saw nothing but something similar to it, so I returned it, and he thought he would be fined."
"28546","(28546) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; There are two men who encouraged another man, and one of them encouraged him in a complete manner, and the other encouraged him explaining clearly. He does not know, nor does he know which of them he encouraged. Al-Muddahiyah, nor which of them is the burden of pain, and he said: On each of them is half the burden, and half of the Mudhahiha."
"28547","(28547) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Khalifa bin Khayyat, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace; He said in his sermon, while leaning his back against the Kaaba, he said: The Muslims will be rewarded with blood. We are the closest to them, and they are a hand over everyone else. (Abu Dawud 2745. Ibn Majah 2685)"
"28548","(28548) Waki’ told us, he said: Abu Al-Ashhab told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Muslims will be rewarded for their blood, they will strive under their protection, and they will be a hand against everyone else.

(Abu Dawud 4519. Ibn Majah 2684)"
"28549","(28549) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Ali ibn Salih, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Qurayzah and al-Nadir were, and al-Nadir was more honorable than Qurayzah, so if a man from Qurayzah killed a man from Al-Nadir was killed for it, and if a man from Al-Nadir killed a man from Qurayzah, his blood money was one hundred wasq of dates. When the Prophet was sent, he prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace. A man from al-Nadir killed a man from Qurayzah. They said: Bring him to us and we will kill him. They said: Between us. And among you was the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So they came to him, and the following verse was revealed: {And if you judge, judge between them with justice}, so justice: A life for a life, then it was revealed: {What is the matter with the ignorant ones who seek?}"
"28550","(28550) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He was among the Children of Israel. Retaliation, but the blood money was not among them, so God said to this nation: “Retaliation is prescribed for you for killing, a free for a free. And the slave for the slave, and the female for the female, so whoever is pardoned from his brother in any way, then he should do what is right and return it to him. With goodness} So pardon: to accept the blood money intentionally: {That is an alleviation from your Lord and His mercy} He said: So he must follow this. with kindness, and he must return to it with kindness. {So whoever commits transgression after that will have a painful punishment} (Bukhari 4498). Ibn al-Jaroud 775)"
"28551","(28551) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: What is his saying: {The free for the free and the slave? By the servant}? He said: A slave kills a slave, like him, and he is rewarded for it, and if the killer were better, they would have nothing but value. The murdered"
"28552","(28552) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Ibn Ash’u, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: It was between Two times there was a battle among the Arabs, and some of them and some of them were killed. Then one of the two times said: We will not be satisfied until we are killed by a woman. The man, and by the man the two men. He said: But the others refused, so they went up to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So he said The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Murder is bad, that is, equal. He said: So the people came to an agreement among themselves over the blood money. He said: So they counted the man’s blood-money as the man’s blood-money, and the woman’s blood-money as the woman’s blood-money, and the slave’s blood-money for the slave. So he made up for one of the two times. On the other hand, he said: It is his saying: {O you who have believed, prescribed for you is retaliation for the murdered. The free for the free, and the slave. for the slave, and the female for the female}"
"28553","(28553) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about sheep that fell in the crops of a people? Hammad said: He is not guaranteed, and Al-Hakam said: He is guaranteed."
"28554","(28554) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; A sheep entered upon a weaver and spoiled his spinning, so Al-Sha’bi did not hold the owner of the sheep liable for the Fire."
"28555","(28555) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id, and Haram bin Sa’d; The she-camel of Al-Bara' bin Aazib entered a people's house and caused harm to them, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided that To protect the property from its owners during the day, and to protect the property from its owners during the night. (Abu Dawud 3565. Ahmed 295)"
"28556","(28556) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Muhammad (H) and Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; A sheep ate dough, and the other said: It was spun by day, so Sharih invalidated it, and recited: {When the people’s sheep scattered therein}, and he said In the hadith of Ismail: The blowing occurred only at night."
"28557","(28557) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Amir, who said: A man came to Shurayh and said: He saw This is when I cut off my flirtation, and he said: By night or by day? If it was daytime, then he is cured, and if it was night, then he is liable, and he recited: {When the people’s sheep scattered therein}, and he said: It was only The blowing occurred at night."
"28558","(28558) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Mara bin Sharahil, on the authority of Masruq; {When the people’s sheep scattered therein} He said: It was a vineyard, so they entered therein at night, but they did not leave anything green therein."
"28559","(28559) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ali, who said: Uthman said: Whoever sits with a blind person, then he becomes infected with him. If a blind person does something, it is a waste."
"28560","(28560) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Hasirah, on the authority of Zaid bin Wahhab; When Ali stoned the woman, he said to her guardians: This is your son, you may inherit from him and he will inherit from you, even if he committed a crime. May you be rewarded."
"28561","(28561) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man curses his wife, separate them, and do not They will never be together, and the child will be joined to his mother’s lineage. They will inherit it and take care of it."
"28562","(28562) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Omar, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: His entire inheritance is for his mother, and it is reasonable The same goes for the child of an adulteress, and the child of a Christian whose mother is Muslim."
"28563","(28563) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’, on the authority of his followers, and Abu Hashim, they said about a man who killed a man intentionally. He was imprisoned to be led by him, then a man came and killed him intentionally. They said: He should not be led by him."
"28564","(28564) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If a man kills intentionally, then the killer kills a man intentionally, He killed the middle man."
"28565","(28565) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Qays ibn Muslim, on the authority of Tariq ibn Shihab, on the authority of Al-Haytham ibn Al-Aswad, On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr; {So whoever gives it in charity, it will be an expiation for him.} He said: He will remove from him any sins like that."
"28566","(28566) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; {So whoever gives it in charity, it will be an expiation for him} He said: for the wounded, and Mujahid said: for the wounded."
"28567","(28567) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Mujahid, who said: It is an expiation for wounds. And the reward of the one who is afflicted is with Allah."
"28568","(28568) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Hasan; {So whoever gives it in charity, it will be an expiation for him} He said: for the wounded."
"28569","(28569) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, saying: I heard him say: If he pardons him, or He takes retaliation from him, or accepts blood money from him, and it is expiation."
"28570","(28570) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Mujahid, who said: An expiation for the one who gives alms to him, and is rewarded. The one who was afflicted by God."
"28571","(28571) Al-Fadl bin Dukain and Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; {So whoever gives it in charity, it will be an expiation for him.} He said: for the transgressor, and the reward of the one who gives charity is from God."
"28572","(28572) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Ammar, on the authority of Abu Uqba, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid; {So whoever gives it in charity, it will be an expiation for him.} He said: for the one who is wounded."
"28573","(28573) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Idris, on the authority of Ubadah bin Al-Samit, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace; He said: You pledge allegiance to me on the condition that you do not associate anything with God, do not commit adultery, and do not steal. So whoever does any of that? So he was punished for it, so it is his atonement. (Bukhari 4894, Muslim 1333)"
"28574","(28574) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: For the one who gives it in charity."
"28575","(28575) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Fudayl, on the authority of Ibn Abi Al-Awja’, on the authority of Abu Shurayh Al-Khuza’i said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever is afflicted with blood or dementia, and dementia means a wound. He has a choice between one of three, and if he wants the fourth, then take his hand. To kill, or to pardon, or to take blood money. Whoever does any of that and then does it again, for him will be the fire of Hell, immortal and immortal. Therein forever. (Abu Dawud 4490. Ahmed 31)"
"28576","(28576) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Hamza Abi Umar, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Wa’il, on the authority of his father, he said: I witnessed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when the murderer was brought and he was being dragged on his knees. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And he handed over to the guardian of the murdered one. Will you pardon him? He said: No. He said: So you take the blood money? He said: No, he said: So you kill him? He said: Yes, so he repeated three times, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: If you pardon him, he will go home. For his sin, he said: So he pardoned, and I saw him dragging his share, he was pardoned."
"28577","(28577) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: A man was killed in covenant. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and this was referred to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he handed it over to the guardian of the murdered man, and he said The killer: O Messenger of God, I did not want to kill him. He said: Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to the guardian: If he is truthful, then You killed him and you entered the Fire. He said: So leave him on his way. He said: And he was wrapped in his Nasa'ah. He said: So he went out dragging his Nasa'ah. He said: So he was named Dhu Al-Nasa'ah. (Abu Dawud 4492. Tirmidhi 1407)"
"28578","(28578) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a free man and a slave who collided and died? They said: As for the blood money of a free man, it is not due on the slave, but as for the blood money of the slave, it is the responsibility of the free person."
"28579","(28579) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah (h) and on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; {And if there is a covenant between you and them}, they said: A man is greeted in a place of war, and the man kills him, not The blood money is upon him, and the expiation is upon him."
"28580","(28580) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; In the Almighty’s saying: {And whoever kills a believer by mistake - the freeing of the slave of a believer and his blood money delivered to his family}, if he is killed The Muslim, then this is for him and his Muslim heirs. {And if he is of a people who are enemies to you and he is a believer}, the Muslim man shall be killed. And his people are polytheists. There is no covenant between them and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he must free a slave. A believer, and if he kills a Muslim from a polytheist people, there will be a covenant between them and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He must free the slave of a believer, and his blood money must be paid to his people who are among them and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings be upon him, a covenant, so his inheritance will be for the Muslims, and his mind will be for his people, the polytheists who are among them. And there was a covenant between the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so the Muslims would inherit his inheritance, and his wealth would be for his people. Because they understand it."
"28581","(28581) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Issa bin Mughiryah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; In his saying: {And if there is a covenant between you and them}, he said: He is one of the people of the covenant, but not a believer."
"28582","(28582) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, saying: Ammar bin Ruzaiq narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abi Yahya. On the authority of Ibn Abbas; {So if he is from a people who are enemies to you and he is a believer, then free the slaves of a believer.} He said: The man used to come to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, and he is greeted, then he returns to his people and he is among them, and they are polytheists, so the Muslims will be afflicted with him. A mistake in his company, or a raid, then he who afflicts it will free his slaves, {even if he is of a people among you. And there is a covenant between them. blood money, and frees the one who struck him upon his neck."
"28583","(28583) Yahya bin Abdul-Malik bin Abi Ghaniyya told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hikam; Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Muttalib slapped a man, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took him away from Abbas, so he pardoned him. (Nasa’i 6977)"
"28584","(28584) Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Masoudi narrated to us: Abd Allah bin Abd al-Malik bin Abi Ubaidah, on the authority of Najiya Abi Al-Hassan, on the authority of his father; That Ali said about a man who slapped another man, so he said to the one who was slapped: Retaliate."
"28585","(28585) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Mukhariq, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab; That Khalid bin Al-Walid forced a man from Murad to slap his nephew."
"28586","(28586) Sharik told us, on the authority of Mukhariq, on the authority of Tariq; That Khalid bin Al-Walid refrained from slapping him."
"28587","(28587) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Shuraih; Indeed, he protected from his blows and scratches."
"28588","(28588) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Shuraih; Indeed, he protected from his blow."
"28589","(28589) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ibn al-Zubayr; Indeed, he protected from his blow."
"28590","(28590) Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Masoudi told us, on the authority of Zurara ibn Yahya, on the authority of his father; Al-Mughirah bin Abdullah refrained from smiting him."
"28591","(28591) Shababi told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Husayn, who said: I heard Tariq bin Shihab, saying: He slapped One day Abu Bakr was a man who slapped him, and it was said: We have never seen him like today. He prevented him and slapped him, so Abu Bakr said: This is He came to me to carry him, so I carried him, and when he was selling them, I swore that I would not carry him: By God, I did not carry him, three times. Then he said to him: Retaliate, so the man pardoned him."
"28592","(28592) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, who said: I said to Ibn Abi Laila: Have you saved from his blow? He said: Yes, and from blows."
"28593","(28593) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq; Indeed, he protected from his blow."
"28594","(28594) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; A helmsman stabbed a man with a whip, but he drove him away with a whip."
"28595","(28595) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Fudail, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mughaffal, he said: I was sitting with Ali, Then a man came to him and he walked with him, and Ali said: O Qunbar. The people said: O Qunbar. He said: Bring this man out and flog him. Then he came. He was flogged, and he said: He has added three more lashes to me, so Ali said to him: What is he saying? He said: He has spoken the truth, O Commander of the Faithful. He said: Take the whip and flog him three lashes. Then he said: O Qanbar, if you flog, do not Count the limits."
"28596","(28596) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, Al-Hakam, and Hammad, they said: He was not struck by a whip or a stick. Or a stone, and it is less than the soul, so it is a pillar, its blood is the fuel."
"28597","(28597) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who borrowed a horse from another man, and he rode it until it died. He said: He is not liable because the man runs his horse."
"28598","(28598) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir; Concerning a man who gave a man a horse and he killed him. He said: He is not liable, unless he is a slave or a boy."
"28599","(28599) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Zuhair told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer; Concerning a man who killed a man whose soul had gone from half his body, he said: He is liable."
"28600","(28600) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Whoever stops his animal on the path of Muslims, or places anything, he is a guarantor of his crime."
"28601","(28601) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Ash’ath; On the authority of Al-Sha’bi (h) and on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Whoever ties an animal on a road is liable."
"28602","(28602) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He did not specify anything concerning the Hashemite."
"28603","(28603) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of his leaders; That Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan ruled in al-Damiyah with two camels, and in al-Bada’i with two camels, and he ruled in al-Multahimah. With three most beautiful things."
"28604","(28604) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning the two slaves, one of them gouging out the eye of his owner. He said: If their value is the same, then it is an eye for an eye, and if If the value of one of them is greater than the other, the more should be replaced by the less."
"28605","(28605) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: The slave kills the slave intentionally, and the one who is killed Better than the killer? He said: There is no master of the murdered person except the one who killed their slave, and there is no one but him. Amr bin Dinar said: They have no choice but the killer of their slave. If they wish, they can kill him, and if they wish, they can enslave him."
"28606","(28606) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ziyad bin Muslim; That a man from the people of India came to the safety of Aden, and a man from the Muslims killed him with his brother, so he wrote about that to Omar bin Abdul Aziz, so he wrote: Do not kill him and take the blood money from him, then send it to his heirs, and he ordered that he be imprisoned."
"28607","(28607) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yusuf bin Yaqoub; That a man of the polytheists killed a man of the Muslims, then he entered safely and his brother killed him, so Omar bin Abd killed him. Al-Aziz asked for the blood money, and made it his responsibility in his wealth, and imprisoned him in prison, and sent the blood money to his heirs from among the people of The war"
"28608","(28608) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Habib Al-Muallem, on the authority of Al-Hasan; A man from among the polytheists performed Hajj, and when he returned, a man from among the Muslims met him and killed him. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded him to do so. And peace be upon him to pay his blood money to his family. (Abu Dawud 367)"
"28609","(28609) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Abu Hurr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Among a people who met the enemy and delayed them for five days, and one of them was killed. He said: The Muslims must be destroyed."
"28610","(28610) Hafs told us, on the authority of Abu Talq, on the authority of his sister Hind bint Talq, she said: I was with wives and a boy. She said: A woman passed by and had intercourse with him. I said: I killed the boy, by God. She said: So ten women witnessed with Ali. I lived with them, so he paid her blood money and supported her with two thousand."
"28611","(28611) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Severeness should not be Anything of blood money, except for camels, and the harshness of female camels."
"28612","(28612) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; Concerning a woman who was struck and had three miscarriages, he said: I see that there is deception in each of them, just as there is in every One of them is the blood money."
"28613","(28613) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: I see sneezing as a sign of dissatisfaction."
"28614","(28614) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Screaming"
"28615","(28615) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, he said: Istihilal is the call or sneeze."
"28616","(28616) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Za’idah, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Istihalal is soundness."
"28617","(28617) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Muslim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Concerning the dead beard, if it is plucked, it does not grow."
"28618","(28618) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said, Omar ibn al-Khattab used to count The slave is against her master if she antagonizes him. Muhammad said: My father made an enemy of Anas Omar."
"28619","(28619) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Harith; A servant came to Ali and his family named him, so he freed him."
"28620","(28620) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a thief enters a man’s house and kills him, there is no harm. Aliyah"
"28621","(28621) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: Kill the thief and I guarantee that none of his followers will follow you."
"28622","(28622) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He found a thief in his house, so I attacked him with the sword. If we had left him, he would have killed him."
"28623","(28623) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, on the authority of Hujar bin Al-Rabi’, he said: I said to Imran bin Husayn: What do you think if someone invades me and wants my life and my property? He said: If someone were to enter upon me and want my life and my property, I would think that it was permissible for me to kill him."
"28624","(28624) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Qaboos ibn Al-Muharriq, on the authority of his father, who said: He came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. A man greeted him and said: O Messenger of God, does this man come to me wanting my money? He said: May God remind him. He said: What if he does not remember? He said: Then seek help from those around you among the Muslims. He said: What if there is no one around you among the Muslims? He said: So seek help from the Sultan. He said: What if the Sultan turns away from me? He said: So fight without your master until you protect your master and be among the witnesses of the afterlife. (Ahmad 294. Tabarani 747)"
"28625","(28625) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: I heard him say: I did not know that any of Muslims refrain from fighting a man who blocks his way, or knocking on him in his house, as a sin because of that."
"28626","(28626) Abbad told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Kill the thief, the harjuri, and the showman."
"28627","(28627) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Ibn Umar attacked a thief with a sword. We left him to kill him."
"28628","(28628) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Talha ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Zaid, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever is killed without his property is a witness. (Abu Dawud 4739. Tirmidhi 1421)"
"28629","(28629) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever is killed without his property is a witness. (Bukhari 2480, Abu Dawud 4738)"
"28630","(28630) Hashim told us, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He who is killed without his wealth. He is a witness. (Ahmad 3051. Tabarani 12442)"
"28631","(28631) Marwan told us, on the authority of Zayd ibn Sinan, on the authority of Maymun ibn Mihran, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever is killed without his wealth is a witness. (Ibn Majah 2581)"
"28632","(28632) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: Ibn Hubayra asked him about reason on the heads of Men, or on gifts? He said: No, but on the heads of men."
"28633","(28633) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: I heard Sufyan say: Reason, retaliation, and pre-emption are upon the heads of men."
"28634","(28634) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Raqba, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; In the case of a stone being placed on a wall and it hitting a person, he said: If the root of the wall belongs to the person who shot it, then he is not liable for what it struck, and in The thing is placed on him from his ownership."
"28635","(28635) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, saying: Ash’ath informed me, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He did not think that a man should take revenge on two men in anything less than his own life."
"28636","(28636) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who used to say: If a woman is killed while she is pregnant A ransom and a reward, even if you do not find it."
"28637","(28637) Muhammad bin Sawa’i told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders; If a woman is killed while she is pregnant, is there anything wrong with her fetus? He said: He was saying: There is nothing in it until you slander it."
"28638","(28638) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Al-Furat; Omar bin Abdul Aziz said: Whichever slave kills another slave intentionally, kill him for it, and the price of the first, take him out of the treasury, So he gave him his master."
"28639","(28639) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Asim, who said: Adi bin Arta, the judge of Basra, wrote to Omar bin Abdul Aziz: I found a dead man in the butchers’ market? He said: As for the murdered man, his ransom is from the treasury."
"28640","(28640) Shababah ibn Siwar told us, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about the detestable person who drives in a mirror? Most of my knowledge is that they said: There is no warranty on him."
"28641","(28641) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Mujalid, he said: Arif of Jinnah told me; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was brought to a prisoner in the winter, and he said to people from Jihanna: Take him and warm him. He said: And the warmth on their tongues was the sign of death, so they went with him and killed him, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked them after that? They said: O Messenger of God, did you not order us to kill him? He said: How did I tell you? He said: You said to us: Take him and warm him. He said: Then he said: I have partnered with you then, understand him and I am your partner.

 He said: I narrated this hadith to Aamir. He said: He spoke the truth, and he knew the hadith."
"28642","(28642) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: A woman vowed that she would be led by a rein. In her nose, her camel fell, and her reins were cut off, so her nose was pierced, so she came to Ali asking for her sanity, so he invalidated it and said : I only vowed to God."
"28643","(28643) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ata’ said: If a man kills another man by mistake and then another intentionally, he said: So he committed the mistake because he had made up his mind before intentionally. A person said to him: He killed intentionally, then he killed by mistake? He said: He should not perform it, because his blood has been blocked."
"28644","(28644) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: A man killed a man intentionally, so he fled but was not able to kill him. He was upon him until he died and left behind money, so I ransomed him for the money of the murdered person. It was said to him: Was the murderer imprisoned until he died? He said: They killed him, imprisoned him until he died in prison."
"28645","(28645) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Muslim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: He was asked about a dead person who was found three years old. Biology His head is in a neighborhood, his feet are in a neighborhood, and his middle is in a neighborhood. Al-Sha’bi said: He sends blessings on the middle, and on the people of the middle. Blood money and qasamah: We did not kill, nor did we know of a killer."
"28646","(28646) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: There is no The money for dinars and dirhams is in large quantities, but the large amounts are for camels."
"28647","(28647) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Al-Fadl, on the authority of Harun, on the authority of Ikrimah; Concerning a man who was killed after taking the blood money. He said: He will be killed. Did you not hear God say: (For him is a painful punishment)?"
"28648","(28648) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The blood money will be taken from him but not He will be killed"
"28649","(28649) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Wahhab, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man whose victim was killed, so he pardoned him, then he went and killed him. Al-Hasan said: He should not be killed."
"28650","(28650) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Jabir; Concerning a woman who became pregnant as a result of adultery, so she was imprisoned to give birth, then she was stoned, then a man entered upon her and killed her. He said: Amer said: I don't know anything about it, other than that the son is the Sultan's, and he rules over it as he pleases.

 He said: And Hammad told me, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: None of the Muslims has more right to it, some of them than others, and Hammad said: There is deception in the child."
"28651","(28651) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, about the owner of the crossing crossing with an animal. Then it sank. He said: There is no guarantee on it."
"28652","(28652) Abd al-Rahim and Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: In his fat. The ear is a third of the money of the ear."
"28653","(28453) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Amir, who said: He disputed with Ali regarding a bull that had gored a donkey. So he killed him, and Ali said: If the bull entered upon the donkey and killed him, then he is liable, but if the donkey entered upon the bull and killed him, then he is liable. There is no guarantee on it."
"28654","(28654) Sharik told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: They retaliate against each other, then the punishments are established, meaning: People hurt each other."
"28655","(28655) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of his father; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Asama: O Asama, do not intercede for anyone, and when he interceded, he would intercede for you. (Ibn Saad 69)"
"28656","(28656) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: He does not intercede for anyone."
"28657","(28657) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Urwa, on the authority of Al-Farafasi, the Hanafi, who said: They passed by Al-Zubair with a thief and he interceded for him. They said: Will you intercede for a thief? He said: Yes, as long as it is not brought to the Imam. If it is brought to the Imam, then God will not pardon him if He pardons him."
"28658","(28658) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Abdullah bin Urwah, on the authority of Al Farafasi, on the authority of Al Zubair. Like him."
"28659","(28659) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman Al-Rawasi told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Abu Hazim; That Ali interceded for a thief, so it was said to him: Will you intercede for a thief? He said: Yes, that will be done unless the Imam is informed of it. If the Imam is informed of it, then God will not pardon him if He pardons him."
"28660","(28660) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Ubaid, on the authority of Suleiman bin Abi Kabshah; That a thief passed by Saeed bin Jubayr and Ata, so they interceded for him, and it was said to them: Do you think that? They said: Yes, as long as it is not brought to the Imam."
"28661","(28661) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Abd al-Wahhab, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Whose intercession is impossible Without any of the limits of God, God has contradicted His creation. (Abu Dawud 3592. Ahmed 70)"
"28662","(28662) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was spoken to about something, and he said: If Fatima had been the son of Muhammad, I would have fulfilled the punishment on her. (Bukhari 34751, Muslim 1315)"
"28663","(28663) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Talha bin Rukan, on the authority of his mother Aisha. Bint Masoud bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of her father Masoud, who said: When the woman stole that piece of cotton from the house of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. We magnified that. The woman was from Quraysh, so we came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. We spoke to him and said: We will ransom her with forty uqiyah. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Purification is better for her. When we heard the words of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, we came to Asama and said: Speak to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace and blessings of God be upon him. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw that, he stood up and preached, and said: How much are you superior to me in any way? From God’s limits, did he fall upon one of God’s female slaves? By the One in whose hand is my soul, if Fatima, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had revealed the same thing with which it was revealed, Muhammad would have cut off her hand. (Ahmad 409. Tabarani 792)"
"28664","(28644) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Harb ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman bin Thawban, on the authority of Zayd bin al-Salt, who said: I heard Abu Bakr al-Siddiq say: If I took a drink, I would love it. That God would cover him, and if I caught a thief, I would love for God to cover him."
"28665","(28645) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Masruq, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: A defect belonging to Ammar was stolen in Muzdalifah. So he placed a veil in his tracks, and called the rhymer, and they said: An Ethiopian. So they followed his tracks until they came to a wall, which is He turned it over, then he took it and left it, and it was said to him? He said: I will protect him. Perhaps God will protect me."
"28666","(28666) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ikrimah; Ibn Abbas, Ammar, and Al-Zubayr captured a thief and let him go. I said to Ibn Abbas: What an evil thing you did when you let him go. On his way, he said: You have no mother, but if it were you, you would be pleased if he cleared your way."
"28667","(28667) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cut off May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, in a shield whose value is three dirhams. (Bukhari 6797 and Muslim 1314)"
"28668","(28668) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Suleiman bin Kathir and Ibrahim bin Saad told us, they all said: Al-Zuhri informed us, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: The pieces are for a quarter of a dinar. Then onwards (Bukhari 2790, Muslim 1312)"
"28669","(28669) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Ezzah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cut off five dirhams. (Abu Dawud 243. Abu Ali 5333)"
"28670","(28670) Ahmad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Wahhab, he said: Abu Waqid narrated to us, on the authority of Aamir bin Saad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The thief will be cut off for the price of a shield. (Ibn Majah 2586. Ahmed 169)"
"28671","(28671) Hatem bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali; He cut off the hand of a thief with a piece of iron, the price of which is a quarter of a dinar."
"28672","(28672) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, he said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Pieces are the price of a shield. (Ahmad 1801, Bayhaqi 259)"
"28673","(28673) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa`id, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, who said: The pieces A quarter of a dinar or more. (Malik 832. Ibn Hibban 4462)"
"28674","(28674) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Humaid, who said: Anas was asked: How long should a thief’s hand be cut off? He said: Abu Bakr has stated that I am not pleased with the fact that I have five dirhams or three dirhams."
"28675","(28675) Waki’ told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas; A man stole a shield during the reign of Abu Bakr and it was cut off."
"28676","(28676) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: The hand will be cut off for the price of a shield. He said: I said: Did he mention its price to you? He said: Four, or five."
"28677","(28677) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Dawud bin Faraij; He heard Abu Hurairah and Abu Sa`id al-Khudri saying: The hand should not be cut off except for four dirhams and more."
"28678","(28678) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Umrah, she said: I learned that Uthman cut his I hope, I value three dirhams. (Malik 832)"
"28679","(28679) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, she said: It is cut in a quarter of a dinar, and Amrah said: It is cut in a piece of water."
"28680","(28680) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: The thief will be cut off at the price of a shield."
"28681","(28681) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroubah (h) and Ismail, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, On the authority of Omar, he said: Do not cut off the fifth except in five cases."
"28682","(28682) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yassar, who said: Do not cut off the fifth except in Five"
"28683","(28683) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father; Ibn al-Zubayr cut two sandals."
"28684","(28684) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: They used to beat each other with whips on the way. Mecca, and Othman said: If you return, I will cut off his wounds."
"28685","(28685) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: May God curse the thief. He steals eggs and his hand is cut off, and he steals rope and his hand is cut off.

(Muslim 1314, Ibn Majah 2583)"
"28686","(28686) Abdul Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Muhammad, who said: A man who had stolen was brought to Uthman. I begged, so he gave her a quarter of a dinar, then he cut off his hand."
"28687","(28687) Abdul-Ala narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: Ayoub bin Musa narrated to me, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: No. The thief will be cut off at less than the price of a jinn, and the price of a jinn is ten dirhams."
"28688","(28688) Abdul-Ala and Abdul-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: He used to say: The price of a shield is ten dirhams."
"28689","(28689) Ibn Mubarak and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, that he said: It is not cut off. Except for a dinar, or ten dirhams."
"28690","(28690) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hamza al-Zayat, on the authority of al-Hakam, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: The value of the Majan is a dinar, which The hand shall be cut off."
"28691","(28691) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdul Malik bin Abi Sulaiman, on the authority of Ata’, he said: The lowest The thief is given the price of a jinn, and the value of a jinn in their time was a dinar, or ten dirhams."
"28692","(28692) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah said: The hand is not cut off except in A shield, or a shield. He said: I said to Abraham: How much is it worth? He said: A dinar."
"28693","(28693) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, who said: He was the thief at the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, was cut off for the price of the shield, and the shield at that time had a price, but it was not cut off for anything. trivial

(Abdul Razzaq 18959)"
"28694","(28694) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: It is cut for an eighth of Madness"
"28695","(28695) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Atiyya ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of al-Qasim, who said: A thief was brought to Umar and he ordered him to be cut off, so he said: Othman: If what you stole is not worth ten dirhams, he said: So Omar ordered it to be stolen, and it was worth eight dirhams, but he did not cut it."
"28696","(28696) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, who said: I entered upon Saeed bin Al-Musayyab and said to him: Your companions; Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri, and Ibn Yasar say: The price of a shield is five dirhams. He said: As for This has passed a year from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Ten dirhams.

(Abdul Razzaq 18951)"
"28697","(28697) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Why He would break the covenant of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding trivial matters. (Bukhari 6792 and Muslim 1313)"
"28698","(28698) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Sulaiman ibn Musa, on the authority of Uthman, who said: He does not have to cut off even He takes the belongings out of the house."
"28699","(28699) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr ibn Shu`ayb, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: He does not have to sever it. Until he takes the belongings out of the house."
"28700","(28700) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Al-Furat, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: It is not cut off. Until he takes the belongings out of the house."
"28701","(28701) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Husayn Al-Harithi, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: He came With a man who had made a hole in his head, and he was taken in that state, but he did not cut it off."
"28702","(28702) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, that he was asked about a man who stole a piece of his property, then rolled it up. So he caught up with you before he left the house? He said: He does not have to cut it off."
"28703","(28703) Ibn Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: He is not required to cut off his belongings until he takes out the belongings from The house."
"28704","(28704) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: The thief will be taken. He has taken the goods, and he has collected them. At home? He said: There is no cutting on him until he comes out with it, they claimed. He said: Amr bin Dinar said: I do not see any cutting on him."
"28705","(28705) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Abi Harb bin Abi Al-Aswad; A thief broke into a people’s house, and the guards caught him and took him. He was brought to Abu Al-Aswad and he said: You found something with him. They said: No, so he said: The wretch wanted to steal, so you hastened him, so he flogged him with twenty-five lashes."
"28706","(28706) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hamid; Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote about a thief: He should not be cut off until he has taken the belongings out of the house, perhaps repentance will occur to him. Before he left the house."
"28707","(28707) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, he said: Aisha informed They say: If he does not bring out the belongings, he will not cut them. She said: If I had only found a knife, I would have cut them."
"28708","(28708) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If he committed adultery, stole, killed, and committed punishment, he said: He will be killed, and nothing more than that."
"28709","(28709) Hafs told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Abdullah said: If two borders meet, one of them will kill, Murder came upon the other."
"28710","(28710) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If boundaries come together, they are both established over him."
"28711","(28711) Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad al-Darawardi told us, on the authority of Hussein bin Hazim, who said: I saw Omar bin Abd al-Aziz hit The neck of a thief, after his quarters were cut off."
"28712","(28712) Ibn al-Darawardi told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of a man from the people of al-Shifa’; Othman bin Affan beheaded Qaynas after his quarters were cut off."
"28713","(28713) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj; He said: Ataa used to say: If he steals and drinks alcohol, then kills, then it is murder, it cannot be cut off, nor should he be punished."
"28714","(28714) Muhammad ibn Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Maliki saying: The punishments shall be established on it. Then he will be killed."
"28715","(28715) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sa’id bin Abi Aroub narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: It will be established upon him. borders, then he is killed."
"28716","(28716) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If there are limits In it there is killing, for killing includes all of that."
"28717","(28717) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; Concerning a man who steals and has his hand cut off. He said: There is nothing wrong with him unless something is found with him. Hammad said: To be continued. With it"
"28718","(28718) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi (h) and Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: There is nothing wrong with him. If his hand is cut off, unless there is something in his eye."
"28719","(28719) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; He said regarding the thief: If the theft is found in his possession, it will be taken from him, and his hand will be cut off, even if he has He consumed it, his hand was cut off, and there is no warranty on him."
"28720","(28720) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; Like him"
"28721","(28721) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The thief will not be fined after cutting off his oath. Unless the theft is found in its own right, in which case it will be taken from him."
"28722","(28722) Sa’l bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to guarantee the thief after he cut him off."
"28723","(28723) Abu Khalid told us, not Al-Ahmar, on the authority of Quraysh ibn Hayyan Al-Ijli, on the authority of Matar Al-Warraq, he said: Saeed was asked Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of a man who steals and his hand is cut off, will he be fined for stealing? He said: It is definitely enough of a fine."
"28724","(28724) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: I entered upon Omar bin Abdul Aziz, and he asked me about Should the absent slave who stole be cut off? I said: I have not heard anything about it. When I came to Medina, I met Salim bin Abdullah, and they told me that Abdullah bin Omar He cut off a slave of his, a thief, an abductor."
"28725","(28725) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, regarding a slave who is left behind stealing. He said: He is cut off."
"28726","(28726) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: It is cut off."
"28727","(28727) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Amir; That Omar bin Abdul Aziz asked Urwah about him? He said: It will be cut off."
"28728","(28728) Aswad bin Amir told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed; Omar bin Abdul Aziz and Al-Qasim said: If an absent slave steals, he will be cut off."
"28729","(28729) Mahboub Al-Qawariri told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khaled Al-Hadha’, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He was asked about a slave who escaped from stealing and having his hand cut off? He said: Yes."
"28730","(28730) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It is not cut off. If an abandoned slave steals, he will be released."
"28731","(28731) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Uthman and Marwan used to say: No. He is cut off."
"28732","(28732) Hammad bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; Othman, Omar bin Abdul Aziz, and Marwan did not cut off a freed slave if he stole."
"28733","(28733) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, and Yahya, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: A slave of Ibn Umar was stolen, so he sent him To Saeed bin Al-Aas, and he said: This man stole, so cut him off. He said: A freed slave should not be cut off."
"28734","(28734) Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Aisha, she said: He does not have to cut it off."
"28735","(28735) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Uthman was brought to a boy who had stolen, and he said: Look at him. Mu'tazariah, has it grown?"
"28736","(28736) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, and Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Othman; In the same way"
"28737","(28737) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ismail ibn Umayyah, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban, who said: He invented A boy from among us had a woman’s hair in his hair. He was brought up to Omar, and he doubted it. He looked at it but did not find it growing. He said: If only I had found you. I grew up because I flogged you, or I cursed you. (Abu Ubaid 289)"
"28738","(28738) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas; A boy was brought to Abu Bakr who had stolen, but his wet dream was not evident. He cuts it off."
"28739","(28739) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Khalas, on the authority of Ali, who said: When the boy reaches puberty Five spans, retaliation from him, retaliation for him."
"28740","(28740) Muhammad bin Bakr narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, who said: A slave was brought to Ibn al-Zubayr. Omar bin Abi Rabi`ah stole, so he ordered it to be done, and it was a span while he was handsome, and it reached six spans, so he cut it off."
"28741","(28741) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his leaders; Omar bin Abdul Aziz and Al-Hasan were not in charge of the boy until he reached puberty."
"28742","(28742) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, regarding a boy who steals. He said: He does not even cut him off. He has a wet dream, and Amr bin Dinar said: I definitely do not see him having a wet dream."
"28743","(28743) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is not cut until it is made of sense. It means he has a wet dream."
"28744","(28744) Muhammad bin Bakr narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, who said: There is no punishment, and no imposition upon whoever does not He fulfills the dream."
"28745","(28745) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Sulaiman ibn Yasar, who said: Omar was brought to a boy who had stolen. So he ordered it to be extended, and he found six inches, except for a fingertip, so he left it, so the boy was named, Namilila."
"28746","(28746) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: Abdullah was given a slave girl who had stolen but did not menstruate, but she did not menstruate. He cuts it off."
"28747","(28747) Abd bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a slave woman, he marries him and has intercourse with her, then she commits adultery. He said: There is no punishment for her until she menstruates."
"28748","(28748) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of the ruling, he said: There is no punishment for a slave woman until she menstruates."
"28749","(28749) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: There is no punishment for a slave woman until she menstruates, or menstruates. To date"
"28750","(28750) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: There is no punishment for a slave woman until she menstruates. Or her menstruation."
"28751","(28751) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Hazm; He brought to him a maid who had not yet reached menstruation, and she took a boy and killed him, and concealed himself from him, so when he saw her, she had deceived him. The great trickster, he ordered her to be killed and she was killed."
"28752","(28752) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr, he said: I heard an alcoholic person saying: When the boy reaches the age of fifteen He is a Sunnah, his testimony is permissible, and punishments are imposed on him."
"28753","(28753) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If he steals repeatedly, then only one hand shall be cut off. If he drinks alcohol repeatedly, and if he slanders it repeatedly, then he is subject to one punishment."
"28754","(28754) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; What is taken regarding a man who has committed adultery with more than one woman, or with more women? He said: One punishment, and the thief is taken after he has stolen many times, like that."
"28755","(28755) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: He used to say, or it is said: If a man steals from various places, Then it was cut off for one person, and it was for them all."
"28756","(28756) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawwi, on the authority of Hammad, who said: If he repeatedly steals, they do not apprehend it. Only after that, for only one hand can be cut off."
"28757","(28757) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: If it is stolen from different parts, and it is cut off for some of them, it is not It will still be cut, unless it results in theft."
"28758","(28758) Omar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If he steals, then steals, then it is brought to him one person, The same applies to adultery."
"28759","(28759) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ibn Shihab said about a man who stole, then he was accused of stealing. Did he steal repeatedly before that, or did he confess to his punishment? He said: His hand shall be cut off, and Ibn Shihab said: Concerning a man who committed adultery and he witnessed it, or he confessed to it, he said: A punishment shall be imposed upon him. One"
"28760","(28760) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hurr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It is permissible for a slave to acknowledge what he has acknowledged regarding a punishment that will be established. upon him, and whatever he acknowledges of what his neck is about is not permissible."
"28761","(28761) Ibn Ayyash told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq; A slave confessed to Shurayh that he had stolen, but he did not stop him."
"28762","(28762) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, and Abdullah bin Isa, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; He said: There is no obligation for a servant to admit to stealing."
"28763","(28763) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, who said: It is not permissible for a slave to confess, except With what we have shown."
"28764","(28764) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It is not permissible for a slave to confess."
"28765","(28765) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu al-Duha and al-Sha`bi, who said: No punishment shall be imposed on a slave. By confession, except with clear evidence."
"28766","(28766) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to say: It is not permissible for a servant to confess to himself if he reaches the soul by mistake, or intentionally."
"28767","(28767) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, he said: The people of Hurmuz and Al-Hayy told me, on the authority of Hormuz, he came to Ali and said: I have committed a punishment, so he said: Repent to God and hide yourself, he said: O Commander of the Faithful, He purified me. He said: Stand up, O Qunbar, and strike him with the punishment, but he will prepare for himself, so if he curses you, then end him. And he was a slave."
"28768","(28768) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mahik; A slave of some of the people of Mecca stole a cloak belonging to Safwan bin Umayyah, and it was brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he ordered it to be cut, and he said: O Messenger of God, will you cut it for the sake of my dress? He said: So come before you bring it to me. (Abu Dawud 4394, Ibn Majah 2595)"
"28769","(28769) Abd al-Rahim bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a servant who steals, he said: He cuts it."
"28770","(28770) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu Bakr bin Abdullah told me, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad; He told him that Abdullah bin Amir told him that Abu Bakr cut off the hand of a slave who stole."
"28771","(28771) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Are there four people who testified against a man for adultery, but one of them was not just? He said: The punishment will be avoided from them because there are four of them."
"28772","(28772) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: If four people testified to adultery, then they were not just. I did not flog them."
"28773","(28773) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If four people testified to adultery against me, They did not treat a man justly, the punishment was spared from him, and none of them were flogged."
"28774","(28774) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of his father, who said: I was sitting at Ali, then a man came and said: O Commander of the Faithful, I have stolen, so he rebuked him, then he came back the second time, and said: I have I stole, and Ali said to him: You have given two witnesses against yourself. He said: So he gave orders for it to be done, and his hand was cut off, and I saw it. Hanging, meaning on his neck."
"28775","(28775) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Ghalib Abi Al-Dhail, who said: I heard seven Abu Salem, he says: I witnessed Al-Hasan ibn Ali and a man was brought to him who admitted to stealing, and Al-Hasan said to him: Perhaps you have embezzled it, in order to He said, “No,” until he acknowledged it twice, or three times, then he ordered him to do so, and he stopped."
"28776","(28776) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, who said: I said to Ata’: A man who testified against himself once. That he stole? He said: It is sufficient for him."
"28777","(28777) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi (h) and Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; They both said: If he slanders a whole people, he will be flogged once, and if he slanders several people, each one of them will be flogged once."
"28778","(28778) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who slanders all people, he said: Every one of them will be flogged to the limit."
"28779","(28779) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who slanders all people together with one slander. He said: There is one punishment for him. And his followers said, on the authority of Al-Hasan: For every man. Some of them are limited"
"28780","(28780) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, who said: One person should be flogged."
"28781","(28781) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he slanders repeatedly, then he slanders it once."
"28782","(28782) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; He used to say: If a man slanders people with one slander, then he is only subject to one punishment."
"28783","(28783) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’, on the authority of his followers, and Abu Hashim; Concerning a man who slandered a whole people, he said: He is subject to one punishment."
"28784","(28784) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who entered upon a household and slandered them. He said: One punishment."
"28785","(28785) Al-Dahhak told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Tawus, who said: One hadd."
"28786","(28786) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hammad, who said: He flogs one person."
"28787","(28787) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father; Concerning a man who slanders all people. He said: If it is in one speech, then it is a single punishment: and if he separates, then it is upon him for each one. Among them is a punishment, and the thief is like that."
"28788","(28788) Hushaym bin Bashir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He said: Whoever slanders a Jew or a Christian, there is no punishment for him."
"28789","(28789) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi; He said something like that."
"28790","(28790) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He was saying that"
"28791","(28791) Abu Muawiyah and Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: The slanderer has no duty to pay. limit"
"28792","(28792) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, Mujahid, Al-Sha’bi (h) and Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, they said: If Judaism and Christianity are under a Muslim, then there is no curse between them, and there is no punishment upon the one who slanders them."
"28793","(28793) Yahya bin Abdul-Malik bin Abi Ghaniyā told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: If he slanders A man is a man, and he has a Jewish or Christian mother, so there is no punishment for him."
"28794","(28794) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If a Jew and a Christian slander, the slanderer will be punished."
"28795","(28795) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Khalda, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: If you were given a man who slandered a Jew, or A Christian and I am a loyalist, I would have beaten him."
"28796","(28796) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He was asked about a man who slandered a Christian woman? He said: He will be beaten if she has a Muslim husband."
"28797","(28797) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab; Concerning Christianity and Judaism, she slanders someone who has a Muslim husband and a child from him. He said: The one who slanders her must have the punishment."
"28798","(28798) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the Jews are And Christianity is under a Muslim man, but a man slandered her, and there is no punishment for him."
"28799","(28799) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Hafs; That a man slandered a Christian woman, who had a Muslim son, so Omar bin Abdul Aziz struck him with thirty-four lashes."
"28800","(28800) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Regarding a Christian slandering a Muslim, he said: He will be flogged eighty times."
"28801","(28801) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Tariq, who said: I witnessed Al-Sha’bi attack a Christian who had slandered an eight-year-old Muslim."
"28802","(28802) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: If a Christian slanders a Muslim, he will be flogged. The limit"
"28803","(28803) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said regarding non-Muslims: They are flogged. Libel against Muslims."
"28804","(28804) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Amir, who said: A Muslim and a Jurmiqani came to me, each one of them had slandered me. One of them was against his companion, so I flogged Al-Jurmaqani, and left Al-Muslim, so Omar bin Abdul Aziz came and mentioned that to him, and he said: Well done"
"28805","(28805) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, who said: I witnessed Al-Sha’abi and he struck a Christian who had slandered a Muslim, so he said: Strike, but do not He sees your armpits."
"28806","(28806) Mukhlid bin Yazid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Omar bin Ata bin Abi Al-Khawar, on the authority of Ikrimah Mawla of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Concerning the slaves, he slanders the freed man. He said: He will be flogged forty."
"28807","(28807) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abi Farwa, on the authority of Makhul and Ata’; Omar and Ali used to beat a slave who slandered a free man for forty."
"28808","(28808) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dhakwan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amer. Ibn Rabi’a, he said: Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, and Uthman Ibn Affan did not flog a slave for slander except Forty, then I saw them add more than that."
"28809","(28809) Abd al-Salam told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: He multiplies forty."
"28810","(28810) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Mu’ashar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He multiplies forty."
"28811","(28811) Abd ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ali, who said: He multiplies forty."
"28812","(28812) Abd ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, and al-Hasan; Like him"
"28813","(28813) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He multiplies forty."
"28814","(28814) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hanzali, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: He multiplies forty."
"28815","(28815) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Hassan, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Forty."
"28816","(28816) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: He strikes forty."
"28817","(28817) Waki` told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, he said: I asked al-Hakam, and Hammad? They said: He will multiply forty."
"28818","(28818) Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Rashid, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: He multiplies forty."
"28819","(28819) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, who said: Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin A slave who was thrown away as a free man eighty years ago."
"28820","(28820) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: He is multiplied by eighty."
"28821","(28821) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul-Rahman, who said: He is multiplied by eighty."
"28822","(28822) Abu Asama told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told me, he said: I read the letter of Omar bin Abdul Aziz to Adi bin Artaa: As for what follows, you wrote asking about a slave who protects a free man, how many times he should be flogged, and you mentioned that it had reached you that I was I flogged him forty lashes while I was in Medina, then I flogged him eighty lashes during my last act, and my first lash was I saw him, and my last flogging agreed with the Book of God, so flog him eighty lashes."
"28823","(28823) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz struck The slave throws eight"
"28824","(28824) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ruzaiq, who said: I wrote to Omar bin Abdul Aziz about a man who slandered his son, Then his son said: If my father is flogged, I will confess, so Omar wrote to him: Flog him, unless he pardons him."
"28825","(28825) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; About a man slandering his son, and he said: He should not be flogged."
"28826","(28826) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who slanders his son, he said: There is no punishment for him."
"28827","(28827) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, who said: Abdullah said: There is no punishment except upon two men: one man. He slandered a married woman, or banished a man from his father, even if his mother was his mother."
"28828","(28828) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If a man negates another man from his father, then it is upon him. The Hadd, even if his mother is a slave."
"28829","(28829) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Sa`id al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who says to another man: You are not of your father, and his mother is mother, or a Jew, or a Christian. He said: He shall not be flogged."
"28830","(28830) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a sheikh from Al-Azd; That Ibn Hubaira asked about him Al-Hasan and Al-Sha’bi? They said: He refers to the hadd, which means that a man is exiled from his father, and his mother is from his mother."
"28831","(28831) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The mother of a child who slanders her should not be flogged."
"28832","(28832) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father (h) and on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin, they said There is no punishment for the one who slanders the mother of the child."
"28833","(28833) Abbad told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who slandered a man whose mother is the mother of a child, he said: There is no punishment upon him until she is freed."
"28834","(28834) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, and al-Shu`bi, who said: Qadhif does not have to do with the mother of the child. Something"
"28835","(28835) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: A slanderer shall not flog the mother of a child."
"28836","(28836) Abbad told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad, who said: There is no punishment for a slanderer who is the mother of a child."
"28837","(28837) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Nafi’; Some of the leaders of the sedition asked Ibn Omar about the mother of a child who was slandered? So he ordered those who threw it to be flogged eighty times."
"28838","(28838) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The one who slanders a mother will be flogged. The boy"
"28839","(28839) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: Ibn Sariha sought refuge, And the son of Umm al-Walad. Ibn al-Sarihah insulted the son of Umm al-Walad and was flogged."
"28840","(28840) Abd al-Wahhab bin Ata’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Yazid al-Madani; Omar bin Abdul Aziz flogged a man who slandered the mother of a man’s son, but she was not freed."
"28841","(28841) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Saeed; That Adaya wrote to Omar bin Abdul Aziz, and he wrote: I will flog him with the punishment of punishment."
"28842","(28842) Ismail bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, who said: I wrote to Abu Qalababi asking him about the woman. It is slandered, even though it was owned? So he wrote to me: The one who slandered her would be given eighty lashes."
"28843","(28843) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning the child’s mother, if she is freed and then slandered, her slanderer shall be flogged."
"28844","(28844) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; He used to say: If a woman is possessed once, then she is freed, then the punishment for her slanderer is due."
"28845","(28845) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of al-Hasan; Concerning a woman who had sexual intercourse with her, then she slandered. He said: The one who slanders her shall not be flogged."
"28846","(28846) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha (h) and on the authority of Mughiry, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, they said: Ali used to say: If the thief steals repeatedly, his hands and feet will be cut off, and then if he returns, I will put him in prison."
"28847","(28847) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: Ali used to do nothing more than cut off A thief has a hand and a foot, and when they are brought to him after that, he says: I am ashamed that he should not purify himself for his prayer, but they caught him. They saved him on behalf of the Muslims, and they spent on him from the treasury."
"28848","(28848) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Abu Bakr decided to cut off the thief. The hand and the foot."
"28849","(28849) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of Makhul; Omar said: If he steals, cut off his hand, then if he returns, cut off his foot, and do not cut off his other hand, and let him eat his offspring. With it he eats food and purifies himself from excrement with it, but keep it away from the Muslims."
"28850","(28850) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The son of Adam is not left like a beast. He has a hand to eat with."
"28851","(28851) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father; That Abu Bakr wanted to cut off the foot after the hand and the foot, so Omar said to him: The Sunnah is the right hand."
"28852","(28852) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha’i, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I saw Omar ibn Al-Khattab He cut off a man's hand after his own hand and foot."
"28853","(28853) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; He was asked: Should a thief be amputated more than one hand and a foot? He said: No, but he will be imprisoned."
"28854","(28854) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: He wrote: We find To Ibn Umar, asking him: Did the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, cut off the man’s hand after the hand? So he wrote to her: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, had cut off the man after the hand."
"28855","(28855) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abdul Rabbo bin Abi Umayyah bin Al-Harith informed me, On the authority of Al-Harith bin Abdullah bin Abi Rabi’ah; He narrated it, and Abd al-Rahman bin Sabit also narrated it. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was brought to a servant who had stolen and cut off his hand, then the second, so he cut off his leg, then he was brought to him. So he cut off his hand, then he was brought to him and he cut off his leg.

(Abu Dawud 247)"
"28856","(28856) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi (h) and on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murah, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Salama; That?? A thief was brought to Ali and he cut off his right hand, then he was brought and he cut off his left leg, then a third was brought. He said: I am ashamed to cut off his hand so that he may eat with it and clean himself with it.

 And in the hadith of some of them: He beat him and imprisoned him."
"28857","(28857) Abu Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Salamah, he said: Ali used to say: Concerning the thief: If he steals, his hand will be cut off, and if he repeats it, his foot will be cut off, and if he does it again, I will put him in prison."
"28858","(28858) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar; Did Najd write to Ibn Abbas asking him about the thief? So he wrote to her with something similar to what Ali had said."
"28859","(28859) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of some of his companions; Omar consulted them about a thief, and they agreed on what Ali said."
"28860","(28860) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Thumama; Anas ibn Malik said that whenever a slave of hiss committed adultery, he would be punished with punishment."
"28861","(28861) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and Zaid bin Khaled and Shibl said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a man asked him about slave mothers committing adultery before they become pregnant? He said: Flog her, and if she commits adultery, flog her. He said on the third or fourth: Sell her, even if it is with braids. (Ahmad 1168; Ibn Majah 2565)"
"28862","(28862) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Abu Jamil, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was informed May God’s prayers and peace be upon him and greeted a mother of theirs who had committed adultery, so he sent me to her and said: Go and perform the punishment on her, so I set off. I found her blood had not dried, so he said: Has she finished? So I said: I found her blood had not dried. He said: If her blood has dried, flog her. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And peace be upon him: And establish boundaries over what your right hands possess.

(Abu Dawud 4468 and Ahmed 89)"
"28863","(28863) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Amr bin Shurahbil, he said: He came Maqil al-Muzani went to Abdullah, and he said: My maid committed adultery, so flog her? He said: Abdullah said: Flog her fifty, so he said: She returned, so he said: Flog her."
"28864","(28864) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ali; Fatima had married her maid."
"28865","(28865) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of Kharijiyah ibn Zaid, on the authority of Zaid; He is the punishment of a female neighbour."
"28866","(28866) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalabab; Abu Al-Muhallab used to flog his female slave if she was immoral in the assembly of his people."
"28867","(28867) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Fudail, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to send for their servants when They flog themselves in the gatherings of adulterers."
"28868","(28868) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to strike his female slave when she was unrighteous."
"28869","(28869) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of his father, who said: I witnessed Abu Barza hit his mother, so she became unjust. He said: And upon her was a veil with which she was wrapped. He said: And with him was a group of people. He said: Then he recited: “And He will witness the torment of them as they gathered.” Of the believers}"
"28870","(28870) Waki’ and Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, He said: I heard the sheikhs of the Ansar say that when a female slave commits adultery, they beat her in their gatherings."
"28871","(28871) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, and Al-Aswad; Indeed, they used to impose punishments on the neighborhood maids when they committed adultery in the gatherings."
"28872","(28872) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: Do not purify yourself in a neighborhood except what you possess. Yemen"
"28873","(28873) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Misra; He used to beat the female slaves of his people and purify them."
"28874","(28874) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, he said: I met Abd al-Rahman bin Maqil, and I said: Have you seen the mother he asked about? Your father, Abdullah, said that she had committed adultery, so he ordered her to be flogged. Did she get married? He said: No."
"28875","(28875) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: If the servant of one of you commits adultery, let him flog her, and if she repeats it, let him flog her. Let him flog her, and if she returns, let him sell her, even if it is for a rope of hair. (Tirmidhi 1440. An-Nasa’i 7240)"
"28876","(28876) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Ibn Abbas (h) and on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid (H) On the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Amr ibn Murr, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, they said: There is no punishment for a mother until she gets married."
"28877","(28877) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Mothers should not be flogged until they are chaste."
"28878","(28878) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The people of Mecca say: When the rains break out and there is no She was married before, and no punishment can be imposed on her."
"28879","(28879) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: There is no penalty for a mother until she is protected. With a husband"
"28880","(28880) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: The definition of offices is the definition of property."
"28881","(28881) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: The limit of offices is the limit of what is owned, as long as nothing remains on it. Writing to him"
"28882","(28882) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Salih bin Hayy, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: The punishment for the owned is what remains on it."
"28883","(28883) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Salih bin Hayy, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The mukatib strikes the punishment of the slave until He is freed"
"28884","(28884) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: His punishment is the punishment of a servant."
"28885","(28885) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ali; In the offices, if he hits someone, he says: He will be struck according to what he paid."
"28886","(28886) Hushaym and Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amir, who said: There is no test in any way."
"28887","(28887) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: The adversity in distress is that it threatens you. He will be brought against him, and if he hits him with just one whip, then there is no confession of anything."
"28888","(28888) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Zayd, on the authority of Wasil, the client of Abu Uyaynah, on the authority of Abu Uyaynah Ibn Al-Muhallab said: I heard Omar Ibn Abdul-Aziz say: Whoever confesses after being struck by a single whip is a liar."
"28889","(28889) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, and Al-Hakam, who said: Al-Mihna is an innovation."
"28890","(28890) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mas’udi, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: Chain is an abomination, imprisonment is an abomination, and the threat Hate"
"28891","(28891) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ali bin Hanzali, on the authority of his father, he said: Omar said: The man is not He is safe from his soul if you make him hungry, or make him afraid, or keep him away."
"28892","(28892) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Shihab said about a man who confessed after he had been flogged. He said: There is no limit to it."
"28893","(28893) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Omar said: Be frightened of the thief and do not be heedful of him."
"28894","(28894) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Tariq Al-Shami; That a man was brought to him who had been caught stealing and he beat him, but he confessed, so he sent to Ibn Umar to ask him about that? Ibn Omar said to him: Do not cut him off, for he only agreed after you struck him."
"28895","(28895) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, who said: I asked him about a man who says to his wife: I did not find you. A virgin? He said: He does not have to do anything, for virginity disappears from leaping, sickness, and prolonged stubbornness."
"28896","(28896) Abd al-Razzaq told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Hakam ibn Aban, on the authority of Salim, who said: I asked him about a man who says to his wife: Why did I find you a virgin? He said: There is no problem, the virgin can be killed by jumping or anything."
"28897","(28897) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Concerning a man who marries a virgin, then says: I did not find you to be a virgin. He said: It is nothing."
"28898","(28898) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He did not see that as slander."
"28899","(28899) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who marries a woman and says: I did not find her to be a virgin. He said: There is no punishment for him."
"28900","(28900) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham, who said: It is not a slander."
"28901","(28901) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Suleiman bin Saar, Ata, and Al-Hasan; About a man saying to his wife, “I do not find you to be a virgin?” They said: The virgin is killed by the sexual intercourse, and by the sexual intercourse."
"28902","(28902) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Al-Haytham, on the authority of the one who informed him, on the authority of Aisha, she said: There is nothing wrong with him, for virginity comes from jumping, menstruation, and ablution."
"28903","(28903) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab; Concerning a man who says to his wife: I do not find you to be a virgin. Sa`id said: Hadd, and do not curse me."
"28904","(28904) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Lahia, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Hubayra, on the authority of a man who named him Zayd bin Thabit and Ibn Umar were asked about a man who said to his wife: I did not find you to be a virgin? They said: If he clears his throat, the hadd will be flogged, and she is his wife, but if he does not clear his name, he will curse her and separate them."
"28905","(28905) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If a man enters the mirror, then he says I did not find her to be a virgin. He said: The punishment should be imposed, but he should not be cursed, because he did not say: I saw you committing adultery."
"28906","(28906) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Shubarmah, who said: I was with Al-Sha’bi, and a man was brought who had been taken for punishment, or He slandered him, and the punishment struck him while he was wearing a shirt. I don’t know what was underneath it."
"28907","(28907) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid (h) and on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The slanderer will be struck. And his clothes are on him."
"28908","(28908) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ismail ibn Umayyah, on the authority of Saad ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of his father, he said: I remember the slaughter of a sheep that my mother ordered it to be slaughtered, when Omar struck Abu Bakr, and he put its tents on its back very hard. multiplication"
"28909","(28909) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The slanderer shall be struck while still wearing his clothes, unless It should be worn with fur or a stuffed cloak until it feels scratched."
"28910","(28910) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abi Malik; That Abu Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah was brought to a man for punishment, so the man went to take off his shirt and said: What should I do for my body? This sinner should be beaten while his shirt was on him. He said: Abu Ubaidah said: Do not let him take off his shirt, so he struck him. Aliyah"
"28911","(28911) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Hammad, who said: The slanderer is struck while his clothes are on him."
"28912","(28912) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: If a man jabs in the winter, he will not wear summer clothes. But he shall be struck in the clothes he ejaculated into, and if he ejaculates in the summer without wearing winter clothes, he shall be struck in the same He threw it into her."
"28913","(28913) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his mother, she said: Indeed, I remember He caught a tea, then mentioned something similar to the hadith of Ibn Aliyah."
"28914","(28914) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Salma bin Al-Majnoon, who said: I said to a man: You who do good to his mother. He said: So they brought me to my father. A kitten and he hit me. He said: The only thing that hurt me was a whip falling upon a whip."
"28915","(28915) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Hay; One of the patient women committed adultery, so her family clothed her with iron armor, so she was taken to Ali, and he beat her and he Aliyah"
"28916","(28916) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Siwar, on the authority of his father, who said: I witnessed Abu Barzah hitting his mother. She was wearing a veil, and she was wearing a veil."
"28917","(28917) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad, who said: As for the adulterer, his clothes should be removed from him, and he recited: {And It will take you with compassion in the religion of God.} I said: This is in judgment. He said: This is in judgment and flogging."
"28918","(28918) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Abi Malik, who said: A man was brought to Abu Ubaidah who had... He committed adultery, and he said: This guilty body deserves to be beaten. He said: So he removed his cloak from it, but he refused to be beaten. He returned his prayers to him."
"28919","(28919) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, who said: A man was brought to Abdullah who was found with A woman in a garment. He said: So he struck them forty. He said: So they went out to Omar and prepared for him, so Omar met Abd. God, and he said: A people who attacked you in such-and-such. He said: So he told him the story, so he said to Abdullah: Is that the case? He said: Yes. They said: We have come to prepare you. Then he asked for a fatwa."
"28920","(28920) Hatim narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, who said: If a man is found with a woman, each one of them will be flogged. A hundred of them"
"28921","(28921) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Salama, on the authority of Al-Hasan Al-Arni, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla; That a man had a husband, and he found him with his wife in a quilt, so he beat him for forty years."
"28922","(28922) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Suwayd bin Najih, on the authority of Dhabyan bin Amara, who said: A man was brought to Ali. And a woman, and a man said: We found them both in one quilt, and with them was wine and perfume. He said: Then Ali said: They are suspicious. They were evil, so he flogged them, but he did not mention any punishment."
"28923","(28923) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Their heads would be cut off and they would be flogged, so he mentioned I will not keep it."
"28924","(28924) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Abu Ruh; That a woman imitated a man’s female slave, and that was at night, so he had intercourse with her while he thought that she was his female slave. He said: That was removed. To Omar, he said: Then he sent for Ali, and he said: Beat the man in private, and beat the woman in public."
"28925","(28925) Ghassan bin Mudar narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Nadhri, who said: Ibn Abbas was asked: What is the punishment for sodomy? He said: He looks at the highest building in the village and throws it backwards, then follows the stones."
"28926","(28926) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Khathim told me, on the authority of Mujahid and Sa`id bin splint; They heard Ibn Abbas say about a man who is found guilty of homosexuality, or is taken into account as a sodomite: that he will be stoned."
"28927","(28927) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of al-Qasim ibn al-Walid, on the authority of Yazid ibn Qays; Ali stoned sodomite."
"28928","(28928) They narrated?? Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man, he comes to a man. He said: His Sunnah is the Sunnah of a woman."
"28929","(28929) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: He who is married or not must be stoned."
"28930","(28930) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The punishment for a sodomite is the punishment for an adulterer, if he is married. Then stoning, and if he is a virgin, then flogging."
"28931","(28931) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A sodomite is in the same position as an adulterer."
"28932","(28932) Zaid told us, he said: Sa’id told me, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan (peace be upon him) and on the authority of Abu Mu’ashr, on the authority of Ibrahim, They said: A sodomite is in the same position as an adulterer."
"28933","(28933) Zaid told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah informed us, on the authority of Hammad bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Ibrahim; Regarding sodomy, he said: If anyone were to be stoned twice, he would be stoned to death."
"28934","(28934) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The sodomite will be stoned if he is married, And if he is a virgin, he will be flogged a hundred times."
"28935","(28935) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of judgment; In the case of homosexuality: he is beaten without punishment."
"28936","(28936) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah bin Muammar, he said: Ali Stoning was killed by Lot's people."
"28937","(28937) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, who said: The anus is greater than the anus. That's it His leaders said: We will stone him to death."
"28938","(28938) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Qais narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn; Othman supervised the people on the day of the funeral and said: Did you not know that it is not permissible to shed the blood of a Muslim except in four cases: a man who has done a deed? Lot's people"
"28939","(28939) Ghassan bin Mudar told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Yazid, on the authority of Sinan bin Salama; He said to him: What a good man he is if he is a homosexual."
"28940","(28940) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos; He used to say: There is no punishment for him, except to say: You are doing the work of the people of Lot."
"28941","(28941) Yahya bin Wadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Al-Dahhak; Like the saying of Tawoos."
"28942","(28942) Zayd bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Khaled Al-Wasiti, on the authority of Al-Shu’abi, he said: I do not know about him. Someone"
"28943","(28943) Abd al-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abi Arouba, on the authority of Farqad al-Sabkhai; That a man said to another man: O faggot, so he asked Al-Hasan and Muhammad? They said: There is no punishment for him, and Al-Hasan said: Unless he says: You are doing the work of the people of Lot."
"28944","(28944) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’, on the authority of his followers, who said: There is nothing wrong with him.

 Abu Hashim said: If he says: You are marrying so-and-so in his anus, he says: Flog him with punishment."
"28945","(28945) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of his followers, who said: A man said to Abu al-Aswad: O faggot, and he said: May God have mercy on Lot, but he did not see anything wrong with him."
"28946","(28946) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Whoever does it and whoever accuses him of it will be flogged."
"28947","(28947) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Whoever slanders a person with it will be flogged, and he seeks it. There are witnesses therein, just as one would like to witness witnesses of adultery."
"28948","(28948) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If a man accuses another of doing the work of the people of Lot, or He was flogged with animals."
"28949","(28949) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abd al-Khaliq, on the authority of Hammad, who said: The punishment is upon him."
"28950","(28950) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Hassan, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Jubayr; That a man said to another man: O faggot, so it was brought to Omar bin Abdul Aziz, and he started saying: O faggot, oh Muhammadi. He said: So he struck him with ten lashes, then he took him out the next day, and he completed the punishment for him."
"28951","(28951) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ikrimah; Al-Hasan said: There is no punishment upon him, and Ikrimah said: There is no punishment upon him."
"28952","(28952) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a man slanders another, the punishment is imposed upon him. If he repeats the slander against him, there is no punishment for him, unless he commits another slander against him."
"28953","(28953) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Uyaynah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father; When Omar ordered Abu Bakra and his companions to be flogged, then Abu Bakra came back and said: Al-Mughirah committed adultery, so Omar wanted to He flogs him, and Ali said to him: What are you flogging him for? And he said nothing but what he had already said, then he left it."
"28954","(28954) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Fudail, on the authority of Ibrahim, regarding a man who slandered A man was flogged, then he slandered him also, and he said: No flogging."
"28955","(28955) Hushaym told us, on the authority of some of his companions, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: There is no right-handed slanderer."
"28956","(28956) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib; Omar bin Abdul Aziz made a man swear to slander."
"28957","(28957) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, who said: Al-Qasim was asked about a man who said to another man: O son of a tailor, or O son of the cupper, or O son of the butcher, and isn’t his father like that? Al-Qasim said: We have overtaken it, and the punishments are not imposed except in clear slander, or in clear denial."
"28958","(28958) Ibn al-Mubarak and Abd al-Razzaq told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Abd al-Karim, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: No. Punishment except for one who sets the punishment as the accusative case."
"28959","(28959) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem; That two men had a quarrel between them, and one of them said to the other: No child of adultery was born in Kufa except that the other was similar to him. The other said: If what the other had had been revealed, I would not have remained in Kufa and dared to do so unless I knew him. So he was asked about that Ash-Sha`bi? He said: There is no punishment for either of them."
"28960","(28960) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’a, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; He did not see any limits in transgression."
"28961","(28961) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no punishment upon him until he says: O adulterer, oh An adulteress, or son of an adulteress."
"28962","(28962) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad; Concerning a man who says to another man: “Indeed, on your back is the punishment for adultery.” He said: If he wishes, he can say: I only said: “Indeed, on your back is a place.” He said: There is no limit to it."
"28963","(28963) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He said: A Hadd shall not be flogged except in the case of clear slander."
"28964","(28964) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Amir, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab; That a man said to another man: O Ibn Karath! He said: The hadd is struck. (Abdul Razzaq 13709)"
"28965","(28965) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ar-Rijal, on the authority of his mother, Amriya, who said: Two men, and one of them said: My mother is not a fornicator, and my father is not a fornicator. So Omar consulted with the people, and they said: He praised his father and his mother, so he said : They had praise other than this, so they struck it."
"28966","(28966) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jald ibn Ayyub, on the authority of Mu’awiyah ibn Qurayh; That a man said to another man: O Ibn Shamah al-Wadhar, so Uthman ibn Affan turned to him and said: I only meant such-and-such, So Othman ordered him to be flogged."
"28967","(28967) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is a punishment in punishment."
"28968","(28968) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: It contains the punishment."
"28969","(28969) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; Samarra said: Whoever rejects, We will reject."
"28970","(28970) Muadh told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abu Raja’; Omar and Othman were punished for satire."
"28971","(28971) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; He saw multiplication as a sign of exposure."
"28972","(28972) Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; He used to flog the punishment in the case of exposure."
"28973","(28973) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Sulayman ibn Yasar, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rabi’i, he said: Omar summoned us regarding young men of Quraysh, regarding female slaves who had committed adultery from the slaves of the Emirate, so we killed them by fifty. fifty"
"28974","(28974) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Amr ibn Sharhabeel, he said: He came Maqil al-Muzani went to Abdullah, and he said: My maid committed adultery, and he said: Give her fifty lashes."
"28975","(28975) Hatem bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a slave confesses to adultery, his master will flog him fifty times. whip"
"28976","(28976) Hatem bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a slave confesses to drinking alcohol, his master flogs him. Forty whips."
"28977","(28977) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: He informed me on the authority of Omar and Othman. And Ibn Omar; They used to beat a slave for wine eighty times."
"28978","(28978) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Ayyub, on the authority of Marouf bin Suwayd; That a people were stealing people’s slaves in Africa, and Ali bin Rabah said: They are not required to cut off their slaves, as it was This is the reign of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, but he definitely did not see them, and he said: These people are stunning."
"28979","(28979) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Whoever steals from a minor will be cut off."
"28980","(28980) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; Whoever steals boys and foreigners: his hand shall be cut off."
"28981","(28981) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ma’n, or Muammar, informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: I asked him about a man who stole a foreign slave? He said: His hand should be cut off."
"28982","(28982) Muhammad ibn Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: I was informed that Omar ibn al-Khattab cut a man’s throat in the case of a boy he stole."
"28983","(28983) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: In A little wine and a lot of wine are eighty."
"28984","(28984) Sa’l bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning alcohol, whether it is little or much, and if it is sweet, then the punishment is imposed on it."
"28985","(28985) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salem, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: Whoever drinks a little bit of wine, or He was struck many times."
"28986","(28986) Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ata’ said: If a man drinks an intoxicant he will not be able to become intoxicated. The punishment has become obligatory upon him."
"28987","(28987) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Husayn bin Abdul Rahman, who attributed it to Umar, saying: Who If he drank a little or a lot of wine, he was hit with the punishment."
"28988","(28988) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no punishment for any drink, even It intoxicates, except with wine."
"28989","(28989) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is mixed with wine for a little while. And many of them."
"28990","(28990) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: Hadd. The wine is eighty."
"28991","(28991) Ibn Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Hassan Ibn Mukhariq, who said: I have heard that a man kept company with Omar Ibn Al-Khattab in He was traveling and was fasting, so when he broke his fast he took refuge in Umar’s waterskin with wine mixed into it that had been trodden by a camel, and he drank. He got drunk from it, so Omar beat him, and said to him: Did you drink from your waterskin? Then Omar said to him: We flogged you because you were drunk."
"28992","(28992) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Regarding someone who is drunk with wine, he said: He will be struck eighty."
"28993","(28993) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The hadd punishment is struck in wine."
"28994","(28994) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Abu Wael, who said: There is no punishment for it."
"28995","(28995) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Aoun, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: In Sugar from wine, eighty."
"28996","(28996) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Dhabi’s brother, who said: It contains the hadd, multiplied by eighty."
"28997","(28997) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: Ali used to provide the people with paint for a sum of money. Children, then a man became intoxicated with it, and Ali gave him eighty lashes. He said: So they bore witness to him that he had only become intoxicated from what He had provided for them. He said : Why did he drink from it until he became intoxicated?"
"28998","(28998) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of Abdullah Al-Danaj, on the authority of Hudayn Abi Sasan; Some people from Kufa rode to Uthman and informed him about the matter of Al-Walid ibn Uqba regarding drinking alcohol. So Ali spoke to him about that, and Othman said: Your cousin is your son, so perform the punishment for him. Ali said: Get up, Hassan. So he flogged him, and he said: Why are you with this? And this changed you. He said: Nay, you have become weak, weak and incapable. Arise, O Abdullah bin Ja’far. So he began to flog you and counted Ali until he reached forty, and he said: Stop, or hold you back. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, flogged forty, and Abu The firstborn was forty years old, and she completed her life at eighty years old, every year. (Muslim 1331. Abu Dawud 4475)"
"28999","(28999) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Omar multiplied the wine by eighty."
"29000","(29000) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ali, who said: A people drank from The people of the Levant used wine, and Zaid bin Abi Sufyan was among them, and they said: It is lawful for us, and they interpreted this verse as: {It is not On those who have believed and done righteous deeds is a reward for what they have eaten. Before they were corrupted by you, when they came to Omar, the people consulted about them, and they said: O Commander of the Faithful, we see that they They have lied about God, and they have practiced their religion unless God has permitted it, so strike their necks, and Ali is silent, so he said: What What do you say, O Abu Al-Hasan, about them? He said: I think that you should ask them to repent, and if they repent, you will flog them eight times for drinking alcohol, and if they do not repent, you will strike their necks. For they had lied about God, and they had practiced their religion unless God had permitted it, so he asked them to repent, and they repented, so he struck them. Eighty eighty."
"29001","(29001) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, he said: Abu Salamah and Muhammad bin Ibrahim told us, Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Azhar, said: A drinker was brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Hunayn. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told the people: “Rise to him.” So the people rose to him and hit him with their sandals.

(Nasa’i 5284 and Hakim 374)"
"29002","(29002) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, saying: Al-Masoudi informed us, on the authority of Zayd al-Ammi, on the authority of Abu Nazrā, on the authority of Abi Saeed Al-Khudri; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, struck the wine with forty sandals, and Omar made a whip in the place of each sandal. (Ahmed 67)"
"29003","(29003) Zayd bin Harun told us, saying: Imran bin Hudayr informed us, on the authority of Al-Sumait bin Umayr, he said: A man entered On the day of Friday prayer, he went to the mosque, prayed four times, and a man said to his companion: Did you see what I saw? He said: Yes, so they took it and brought it to Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari, and they said: This man entered the mosque and prayed four times, so he said: Is this man? He changed? They said: No. He said: This is something I doubt. He said: What made you do what you did? He said: I did not drink it before today, so he was given eight lashes."
"29004","(29004) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Zaid al-Ammi, on the authority of Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace; He mixed the wine forty times. (Tirmidhi 1442, Ahmad 32)"
"29005","(29005) Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, he said: Abd al-Hakim bin So-and-so bin Ya’la narrated to me, on the authority of his father; That Ali bin Umayyah said to Omar bin Al-Khattab, or wrote to him: We are bringing a people who have drunk, so upon whom shall we judge? The limit? He said: Have the Qur’an recite to him, and throw his cloak between his cloaks. If he has not read the Qur’an and does not know his cloak, then stand. May the punishment be upon him."
"29006","(29006) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, he said: Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Utbah narrated to us, saying: I see him mentioned. On the authority of Omar, he said: There is no punishment except for what the mind has hidden."
"29007","(29007) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Utba, on the authority of Abdullah bin Utba, who said: I see it on the authority of Omar, he said: There is no punishment except for what the mind has hidden."
"29008","(29008) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Sa’id, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If a Muslim steals wine from a non-Muslim, he will be cut off. And if he steals it from a Muslim, it is not cut off."
"29009","(29009) Hafs told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amer; Shurayh guaranteed a Muslim’s wine which he spilled to a non-Muslim."
"29010","(29010) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Whoever steals from a Jew, or a Christian, or He took it from the people of the people of Dhimma, it was cut off."
"29011","(29011) Muammar bin Sulaiman Al-Raqqi told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abdul-Jabbar bin Wa’il, on the authority of his father, who said: A woman was forced to marry the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the punishment was averted from her. (Tirmidhi 1453 and Ibn Majah 2598)"
"29012","(29012) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; Omar was brought with some of the slave girls of the Emirate, and two of the slave girls of the Emirate forced them, so the boys were beaten but he did not beat the female slaves."
"29013","(29013) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’; That a man hosted a family member, but one of them disapproved of him, so that matter was reported to Abu Bakr, so he beat him and banished him, but he did not He hits the woman."
"29014","(29014) Muammar bin Sulaiman Al-Raqqi told us, on the authority of Hajjaj; An Ethiopian forced one of their women to force her, so Omar bin Abdul Aziz imposed the punishment on her, and freed her from his neck."
"29015","(29015) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, Al-Shu’abi, and Al-Hasan, they said: There is no punishment for a detested person."
"29016","(29016) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Al-Zuhri, who said: There is no punishment for a person who detests it."
"29017","(29017) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hurr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A slave forced a woman to have intercourse with her, so they disputed. To Al-Hasan, who was a judge at that time, so the punishment struck him, and he ruled that the slave of the woman should be punished."
"29018","(29018) Shabab bin Siwar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a slave-owner who plucked up his slaves? They said: He is subject to punishment, but he is not required to pay zakat."
"29019","(29019) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad, who said: If a drunkard kills, he will be killed."
"29020","(29020) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: He will be killed."
"29021","(29021) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed; That two drunkards killed one of them, he said: Then Muawiyah killed him."
"29022","(29022) Abd al-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, and al-Zuhri, who said: It is permissible to divorce a drunkard, and it shall be cut off if he steals."
"29023","(29023) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hanzali ibn Abi Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Qasim; He was asked about a drunkard who steals? He said: If he was known to steal before that, then cut him off, otherwise no."
"29024","(29024) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salem, on the authority of al-Sha’bi; In Al-Nashwan: He will be cut off if he steals, and he will be held accountable for all his crimes."
"29025","(29025) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; Concerning a drunkard: If he is freed or divorced, then it is permissible for him and the punishment is imposed on him."
"29026","(29026) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If he steals, he will be cut off, and if he kills, he will be killed."
"29027","(29027) Abd al-Salam told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The drunkard did not speak of anything that was established over him."
"29028","(29028) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad, who said: If he steals, he will be cut off."
"29029","(29029) Abdou told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Four to the Sultan; Zakat, prayer, punishments, and the judiciary."
"29030","(29030) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Jabali ibn Atiyya, on the authority of Ibn Muhayriz, he said: Collection, punishments, zakat, and fayy to the Sultan."
"29031","(29031) Omar bin Ayyub told us, on the authority of Mughirah bin Ziyad, on the authority of Ata’ al-Khurasani, he said: To Sultan Zakat, And the combination, and the limits."
"29032","(29032) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: The Sultan is the guardian of those who fight religion. And if he kills a person’s brother or father,"
"29033","(29033) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who said to another man: You drinker of alcohol. He said: There is no punishment for him."
"29034","(29034) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who says to another man: You drink alcohol, you are a drunkard. He said: He did not see any punishment for him."
"29035","(29035) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, about a man saying to another man: O drinker, O thief, He said: There is no punishment for him, but there are lashes."
"29036","(29036) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, he said: We asked Omar bin Abdul Aziz On the authority of a man who said to another man: You drinker of alcohol, or you polytheist, or you drunkard. We said: Is he one? He said: Glory be to God, no one is punished except the one who slanders a Muslim."
"29037","(29037) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer; Concerning a man who says to another man, “You drinker of alcohol.” He said, “Do not hit me.”"
"29038","(29038) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; About a man who cursed his wife, so he separated them, then he lied to himself, saying: He will be flogged, and the child will be attached to him."
"29039","(29039) Hafs told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; Concerning the cursed one, he lies about himself. He said: He is struck while he is engaged."
"29040","(29040) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, who said: If a man slanders his wife, he curses her, then if he lies After that, he was flogged, the child was attached to him, and his wife was returned to him."
"29041","(29041) Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning the cursed man, he lies about himself. He said: The punishment will be flogged."
"29042","(29042) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam. He said: I asked him about a man who curses his wife, then acknowledges the child? He said: The punishment is struck, and the child is attached to it."
"29043","(29043) Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who slanders his wife, or denies his wife’s children, then he lies to himself. He said: He deceives."
"29044","(29044) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Shubarmah, on the authority of Al-Harith (h) and on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ataa (h) and on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; Concerning the cursed one, he denies himself. They said: He will be struck."
"29045","(29045) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: If a man curses, and he refuses The woman is to be cursed and stoned."
"29046","(29046) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: You shall be imprisoned."
"29047","(29047) Abd al-Rahman al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of al-Dahhak; Concerning a man who slanders his wife but she refuses to curse him. He said: She will be flogged and stoned."
"29048","(29048) Omar told us, on the authority of Issa al-Khayyat, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: Whoever is cursed and refuses to swear, it will be imposed on him. The limit

 Issa said: I heard the unpopular saying: They are forced to curse, and they are imprisoned until they curse us."
"29049","(29049) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mutarrif, and Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi (h) and on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Layth, on the authority of Mujahid and Ataa, they said: If he is warded off from cursing, a child will be attached to him."
"29050","(29050) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who curses his wife, then slanders her. He said: He hits, and Amer said: He does not hit."
"29051","(29051) Shabab bin Siwar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a man who curses his wife, then She gives birth, and he says: This is not from me? They said: He will be beaten."
"29052","(29052) Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If I curse her, then he slanders her, there will be no punishment for her. He said: I said: How could he, when he lied to himself? He said: There is no limit, he has cursed me in the Book of God."
"29053","(29053) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the flogged man slanders his wife, he will be flogged, and no He cursed between them.

 He said: I asked Al-Hasan and Aamir? They said: Cursed!"
"29054","(29054) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Mansour, and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man slanders His wife, and he was flogged, flogged, and not cursed, because his testimony is not permissible."
"29055","(29055) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Omar bin Amir, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man lies to himself As long as nothing remains of her curse, he flogged his wife."
"29056","(29056) Abbad told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, the same."
"29057","(29057) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: If he tells himself a lie before the curses end. He will be flogged along with his wife, but if he tells a lie to himself after being cursed, then there is nothing wrong."
"29058","(29058) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of a statement, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, who said: Whoever slanders Ibn Al-Mala’nah, or slanders his mother, will be struck."
